(22, '2010-05-03', '03:05:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping, Jr', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0022-10 of Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping Jr. ?Creating Disaster Preparedness Risk Management Office (DPRMO) in the City of Baguio.?', '-none-', '(NOTE:  [a]  FIRST READING ? 15 March 2010\r\n             [b]  SECOND READING AND FOR PUBLICATION BY POSTING ? 26 April 2010\r\n       - Posted in the bulletin boards of City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library and the Health Services Office starting 28 April 2010.) (Item 41, 28 June 2010 Agenda)', 'Committee on Laws', '1st', NULL, '0557-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends APPROVAL ON SECOND READING AFTER POSTING of the above stated proposed ordinance. (CR NR. 0557-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Deferred - returned to the committee for further study and for the committee to find out if the above proposed ordinance is in accordance with RA 10121 [AN ACT OF STRENGTHENING THE PHILIPPINE DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT SYSTEM, PROVIDING FOR THE NATIONAL DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT FRAMEWORK AND INSTITUTIONALIZING THE NATIONAL DISASTER RISK REDUCTION AND MANAGEMENT PLAN APPROPRIATING FUNDS THEREFOR AND FOR OTHER PURPOSES] and its Implementing Rules and Regulations (23 Aug 2010, 2)', '7th', NULL, 'Pending; Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation, 5th Ind, 07 Jul 2010;', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(23, '2010-05-03', '03:10:00', '-none-', 'Unnumbered Resolution', 'Cabinet Hill-Teachers? Camp Barangay', 'Unnumbered Resolution, series of 2010, of Cabinet Hill-Teachers? Camp Barangay, entitled ?A resolution respectfully calling for the conduct and strict implementation of Barangay Cabinet Hill-Teachers? Camp general assembly on March 13, 2010 from 8:00 to 1', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Barangay Affairs', '1st', '2010-08-03', '00236-10', 'The Committee on Barangay Affairs recommends that the above resolution be NOTED. (CR NR. 00236-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-05-04', 'NOTED', '3rd', '2010-06-04', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(24, '2010-05-03', '03:15:00', '-none-', 'Sworn complaint-affidavit', 'Ms. Reyna Florendo, et al., all residents of Guisad Surong Barangay', 'Sworn complaint-affidavit dated 05 March 2010 filed by Ms. Reyna Florendo, et al., all residents of Guisad Surong Barangay, Baguio City, against Punong Barangay Orlando Soriano, of the same barangay.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above case is docketed as Barangay Adm. Case No. 04-2010.)', 'Division I (Ad Hoc Committee on Barangay Administration Cases)', '1st', '2010-05-03', 'DIV1-2013-004', 'Based on the records, a complaint was filed by Ms. Reyna Florendo et al. on February 25, 2010. The case was docketed as BAC-2010-00224: (BA Case 04-10).\r\nSince the alleged illegal act was committed sometime on 2010, upon the re-election of PB Soriano in the 2010 elections, the case filed against the herein respondent PB Soriano shall be DISMISSED based on the following grounds:                                   \r\n1.  Baguio City Council Resolution No. 96-2011 DISMISSING ALL PENDING ADMINISTRATIVE CASES FILED AGAINST THE BARANGAY OFFICIALS WHO WERE RE-ELECTED DURING THE RECENTLY CONCLUDED BARANGAY ELECTIONS x-x-x-x-x-x-x-x                                                      2.   AGUINALDO DOCTRINE (Aguinaldo vs. Santos GR No. 94115 August 21, 1992) \"x-x-x When the people have elected a man to office, it must be assumed that they did this with knowledge of his life and character, and they disregarded or forgave his fault or misconduct, if he had been guilty of any. X-x-x-x-x-x                                                                                                                                                                                                                      In view thereof, this Division recommends that:                                                                                                                                                                                                                             1.  The parties be furnished with a copy of SP Resolution No. 096-2011 DISMISSING Barangay Case No. 04-10. (DIV1-2013-004);', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Barangay Case Resolution - DISMISSED (22 Jul 2013, 8);', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(25, '2010-05-03', '03:55:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'Upper Quezon Hill Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 10, series of 2010, of Upper Quezon Hill Barangay, entitled ?A resolution requesting the Honorable Members of the City Council to transfer the location of the approved barangay project the road improvement and alleys from Silver St', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Works', '1st', '2010-08-03', '0638-10', 'The Committee on Public Works recommends that the approval of the request of Upper Quezon Hill Barangay ?to transfer the location of the approved barangay project the road improvement and  alleys from Silver Street to Bronze Street in the amount of Php250,000.00 funded from 20% Local Development fund of 2008?, it appearing that such transfer is the wish of Upper Quezon Hill Barangay as manifested in its Resolution Numbered 10, series of 2010, that being the wish of the barangay, as evidenced by attached Resolution Numbered 10, series of 2010.\r\n        The committee further recommends that its docket be cleared thereof and the matter be returned to the City Secretary, Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio, for his referral to the appropriate departments/offices of the city government in order that the immediate implementation of the project may be put in motion. (CR NR. 0638-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved; Ord-56s2010 (23 Aug 2010, 31)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(26, '2010-08-03', '09:55:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0024-10 of then City Councilor Rocky Thomas A. Balisong ?Repealing its entirety Ordinance No. 423, series of 1965 as amended.?', '-none-', '(NOTE: [a] Ordinance No. 423, series of 1965, further amended Section One of Ord. 66, as amended by Ord. 329 and further amended by Ord.418.\r\n-  Ord. 66, series of 1948, prohibited the use of motorcycles or tricycles on the roads, streets, or bridle paths within city limits except on specified areas.\r\n- Ord. 329, series of 1960 which included the exclusive use of motorcycles, tricycles, scooters, bicycles and motorbikes for the delivery of messages by telegram, telephone, radio and other communications services which has branch offices in the City of Baguio.\r\n-  Ord. 418, series of 1965 further amended Ordinance Numbered 329, series of 1960.\r\n- Ord. 423, series of 1965 further amended Ordinance Numbered 418, series of 1965 to include newspaper delivery and newspaper agencies and/or their representatives.)  \r\n[b] [1] FIRST READING ? 15 March 2010		\r\n     [2] SECOND READING AND FOR PUBLICATION AND POSTING ? 26 April 2010\r\n-    Published in the Sunstar issue of 01 May 2010 and was also posted in the   bulletin boards of City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library    and the Health Services Office starting 14 April 2010.)', 'Committee on Laws', '1st', NULL, '0550-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends APPROVAL on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION and POSTING of the above stated proposed ordinance.  \r\nHon. Elmer O. Datuin, Member of the Committee, signified, ?recommends public hearing?. (CR NR. 0550-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Returned to the committee for the committee to conduct a public hearing at its level and to invite the TTMC and the Traffic Management Division of the Baguio City Police Office (BCPO) (16 Aug 2010, 11)', '7th', NULL, 'Pending; Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendatio, 5th Ind., 07 Jul 2010;', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
