(33, NULL, '08:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Codification Committee', 'Letter dated 12 May 2010 of the Codification Committee on Investment Code and Market Code, submitting a copy of the codified Tax Code which includes the Market Code.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '2nd', NULL, '0297-12', 'The Committee on Laws recommends approval of the revisions to City Ordinance Numbered 35, series of 2008 entitled, ?Establishing the Baguio City Investments and Incentives Code (BCIIC)? as embodied in the letter dated 22 November 2011 of the Members of the Technical Working Group (TWG) assigned to review and update the (BCIIC).\r\n             The Committee further recommends that the revisions be considered as Proposed Amendments [PO 047-12] to Ordinance No. 35, series of 2008, and be APPROVED ON FIRST READING, to be authored by willing Members of the City Council and the Presiding Officer. (CR NR. 0297-12)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2012-11-06', 'Related to Proposed Amendment [PO 047-12] to Ordinance No. 35, series of 2008, and APPROVED on FIRST READING and referred to the Committee on Laws (11 Jun 2012, 48.2); Investment Code - referred to the Committee on Laws; Market Code - referred to the Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce (19 Jul 2010, 20)', '2nd', NULL, 'Acted upon; Related to Proposed Amendment [PO 047-12] to Ordinance No. 35, series of 2008, and APPROVED on FIRST READING and referred to the Committee on Laws (11 Jun 2012, 48.1);', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(34, NULL, '01:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Delia G. Fronda, General Manager and Ms. Jocelyn M. Salvado, Vice Chairman and Chairperson, Registration, Qualification and Membership Committee, UNLAD Housing Cooperative (UHC)', 'Letter dated 20 April 2005 of Ms. Delia G. Fronda, General Manager and Ms. Jocelyn M. Salvado, Vice Chairman and Chairperson, Registration, Qualification and Membership Committee, UNLAD Housing Cooperative (UHC) seeking assistance for them to be given opp', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Houising', '1st', NULL, '0542-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above matter BE NOTED, it being a request 5 years ago and may have been overtaken by events. (CR NR. 0542-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (26 Jul 2010, 27)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(35, '2007-06-09', '03:10:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Dr. Florence G. Reyes, MD MPH MSc, City Health Officer, Health Services Office', '1st Indorsement dated 31 August 2007 of Dr. Florence G. Reyes, MD MPH MSc, City Health Officer, Health Services Office, transmitting to Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. the undated letter of Dr. Jennifer A. Bautista, President (2006-2007) and BCDS', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '0543-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above matter BE NOTED.  Accommodating the above private institution may open the floodgate for all other institutions/organizations to request from the City Government any possible government property for their operation.  Further, as per approved plan of the CHSO, there appears no space for another building. (CR NR. 0543-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (26 Jul 2010, 28)', '5th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(36, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. James Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Jeepney Operators, Drivers Association (LATJODA)', 'Letter dated 16 June 2010 of Mr. James Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Jeepney Operators, Drivers Association (LATJODA), in reply to the request of the Sangguniang Panlungsod for them to submit their position paper regarding the request of jeepney associat', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '-none-', NULL, '0620-10', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation encourages ?off street parking? because it is one of the solution to traffic problem within the Central Business District. Likewise, the Traffic Management Branch (TMB) of the Baguio Central Police Office (BCPO) offers no objection to the said request as it will not affect traffic along Abanao Street considering that limited units will only be allowed at the Abanao Shell station as the loading and unloading area and Naguillian shell Station (fronting Camp Allen) as staging area.\r\n         In view of this consideration, the committee recommends to approve the request of the LATJODA to use Abanao Shell station as its loading and unloading area and Naguillian Shell station as staging area subject to the following conditions:\r\n1. That only two (2) units will be allowed to use the said loading area at Abanao Shell station;\r\n2. That three (3) units will be allowed to use Naguillian Shell station (fronting Camp Allen) as staging area;\r\n3. That the LATJODA must maintain order and cleanliness at all times and comply with the provisions of the Memorandum of agreement (MOA);\r\n4.  That the use of the said area will only be good for one month renewable on monthly basis. Provided however that in the event that the use will aggravate traffic along Abanao Street, the city, thru Traffic Management Branch (TMB) will advise LATJODA to look for another ?off street parking? with one week from notice. (CR NR. 0620-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Deferred - returned to the Committee for further study; with Related Motion of Hon. BLFT - Res-196s2010 (23 Aug 2010, 22b)', '4th', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(37, '2009-02-07', '01:20:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong and Hon. Joel A. Alangsab (Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation)', '1st Indorsement dated 01 July 2009 of then City Councilor Rocky Thomas A. Balisong and Hon. Joel A. Alangsab (Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation) forwarding the following to be transmitted to the Committee on Laws as the', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '7th', '2010-07-07', '0554-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends to reiterate again its previous recommendation to adopt the recommendation of Atty. Federico J. Mandapat Jr., Regional Director of the Department of Transportation and Communications Cordillera Administrative Region, ?that the issue be resolved and be put to rest for the greater good of the riding public? as embodied in his letter to the Chairman of the Committee on Laws dated 26 October 2009 ?for item a only.? (CR NR. 0554-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Returned to the committee for further study (16 Aug 2010, 14b)', '9th', NULL, 'Pending; Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommenation, 7th Ind 07 Jul 2010;  [Formerly indorsed and referred to the same committee, 2nd Ind, 06 Jul 2009]', 'Laws 2009', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(38, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'then Councilor Hon. Faustino A. Olowan', '1st Indorsement dated 23 November 2004 of then Councilor Hon. Faustino A. Olowan forwarding the petition dated 15 November 2004 of Punong Barangay Bobby P. Tangalin, et al., Guisad Surong Barangay on the on going construction of a house without a building', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '0744-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above matter be NOTED considering the long period lapsed and the actions of offices concerned. (CR NR. 0744-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (13 Sep 2010, 34)', '4th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(39, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Presentation', 'Engr. Ruben H. Luyon of the Ace Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation', 'Presentation by Engr. Ruben H. Luyon of the Ace Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation during the 19 April 2010 Regular Session re: Productive use of  ?wasted? materials resources through efficient use of ecotechnology.', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '0837-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection recommends that the above be held in abeyance considering the recommendations of Ms. Cordelia C. Lacsamana, Department Head II, City Environment and Parks Management Officer which is hereto attached and which is self explanatory. (CR NR. 0837-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-08-11', 'HELD IN ABEYANCE (08 Nov 2010, 53c)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(40, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Genoveva S. De Vera, et al., residents of Zamora and Bagong Lipunan Barangay', 'Letter dated 01 March 2002 of Ms. Genoveva S. De Vera, et al., residents of Zamora and Bagong Lipunan Barangay requesting segregation of a portion of land which is an excess lot adjacent to their property where their building stands described under TCT No', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', NULL, '0442-11', 'Prior to further action on the above request, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends the following:\r\n     1. For the conduct of relocation/structural survey to determine the actual location of the buildings and the possible road right-of-way of inner lots by the petitioners and at their own expense;\r\n     2. For the petitioners to secure the consent of affected adjacent inner lot or property owners; and\r\n     3. For the petitioners to secure the approval of the court, for the conversion of the land use of the subject lot from road to an alienable and disposable/residential lot as per annotation of TCT No. T-55718. Any favorable action by the court, however, does not construe approval by the City Council of the above request. (CR NR. 0442-11)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved CR (15 Aug 2011, 18)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(41, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'East Bayan Park Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 09, series of 2010, of East Bayan Park Barangay, entitled ?A resolution requesting the Honorable City Council thru the Assessor?s Office to include the following Lot Numbers 006-010 former Barrio Obrero under the jurisdiction of Ea', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', NULL, '0729-11', 'Pursuant to Resolution Numbered 341, series of 2011 ?Requesting the 128 Barangays of the City of Baguio to submit to the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio the description of their barangay political boundaries, in a narrative form approved by their respective Barangay Councils and with the conformity of the adjacent barangays communicated through a Barangay Council Resolution?. The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above request BE RETURNED to the barangay for appropriate action as provided for by Resolution No. 341, series of 2011. (CR NR. 0729-11)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'RETURNED to East Bayan Park Barangay thru Punong Barangay Felipe Gabriz, Baguio City, for appropriate action as provided for by Resolution No. 341, series of 2011 (14 Nov 2011, 50)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(42, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao', 'Letter dated 12 February 2007 of Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao, seeking reconsideration to override the veto message of then Hon. Acting City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. on Res. No. 314, s. 2006.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matters are related to the following:\r\n[a]    The letter dated 10 January 2007 of Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao, submitting his observations relative to the veto message of then Hon. Acting City  Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. on Resolution Numbered 314, series of 2006 and requesting the Honorable Body to exercise again its solomonic wisdom against the veto message of His Honor regarding the same was forwarded to the Committee on Laws on 12 January 2007.\r\n[b]  1st Indorsement dated 08 January 2007 of Mr. Eduardo G. Gamayon, Supervising Administrative Officer, Office of the City Mayor forwarding Resolution No. 314, series of 2006, inviting attention to the veto message made by then Hon. Acting City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. This was forwarded to the Committee on Laws on 09 January 2007.\r\n[c]   Res. No. 314, s. 2006 approved the appeal of Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao for the issuance of business permits to operate at Building II, Maharlika Livelihood Center, earlier revoked through Administrative Order No. 130, series of 2006.) (Item 31, 26 February 2007 Agenda)', 'Committee on Laws', '-none-', NULL, '0300-12', 'Section 55 of the Local Government Code of 1991 provides that, the Local Chief Executive may veto an ordinance or a resolution adopting a local development plan and public investment program.\r\n            Resolution Nr. 314, series of 2006 entitled, ?Approving the appeal of Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao for the issuance of business permits to operate at Building II, Maharlika Livelihood Center, earlier revoked through Administrative Order No. 130, series of 2006? is NOT a resolution adopting a local development plan and public investment program which therefore, may not be the subject of the veto power of the Local Chief Executive as provided for by law.\r\n          Wherefore, the Committee on Laws recommends that Resolution Nr. 314. series of 2006 be considered as valid and subsisting, and the Veto Message of then Hon. Acting City Mayor  Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., be  NOTED. (CR NR. 0300-12)\r\nThe Committee on Laws recommends reiteration of the previous Committee on Laws? recommendation for item b, to override the veto of  Hon. Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., then, Acting City Mayor of Baguio as contained in its 2nd indorsement dated 22 February 2007. (CR NR. 0175-12)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to Atty. Melchor Carlos R. Rabanes, OIC, City Legal Office, Baguio City, for legal opinion on whether or not Resolution Nr. 314, series of 2006 [approved the appeal of Mr. Pablo L. Palangdao for the issuance of business permits to operate at Building II, Maharlika Livelihood Center, earlier revoked through Administrative Order No. 130, series of 2006] is valid and subsisting considering the following sections of Tax Ordinance No. 2000-001:\r\n     [a]  Section 139 prohibited selling or serving intoxicating liquor in stall, booth or store; and\r\n     [b]  Section 134 considered part of the Public market and the Maharlika L:ivelihood Center (Buildings 1 and 2) subject to existing contracts governing them (25 Jun 2012, 37b); Unfinished (18 Jun 2012, 38b); Unfinished (11 Jun 2012, 50b); returned to committee for further study (21 May 2012, 20b); Unfinished (14 May 2012, 22b); Unfinished (07 May 2012, 26b); Unfinished (23 Apr 2012, 39b)', '9th', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(43, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 049-04 of Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as ?Prohibiting politicians and/or public officials from affixing their names on any public structure, equipment, vehicles and properties belonging to the government of Baguio City, otherwise known a', '-none-', '(Item 51, 11 August 2004 Agenda)', 'Committee on Laws', '-none-', NULL, '0271-12', 'Considering that the above proposed ordinances are identical, the  Committee deemed it proper to suggest to the proponents to consolidate their proposals, which was immediately attended to.\r\n              Wherefore, the Committee on Laws recommends  that the attached consolidated and amended proposed ordinance be approved on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION.\r\n(CR NR. 0271-12)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'approved on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION (25 Jun 2012, 25b); Unfinished (18 Jun 2012, 26b); Unfinished (11 Jun 2012, 37b); Unfinished (04 Jun 2012, 41b);', '-none-', NULL, '[Related to Proposed Ordinance [consolidated] of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as and Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Prohibiting politicians and/or public officials from affixing their names or initials and/or images/pictures on any public structures and properties, equipment, vehicles and programs/projects of the City Government of Baguio, otherwise known as ?The No-naming and No-signage of Public Works and Properties Ordinance?.?; Acted upon; Ord-33-2012]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(44, '2010-08-03', '02:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0053-10 of Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Requesting the Office of the Solicitor General to commence reversion and cancellation proceedings to annul Transfer Certificate of Title bearing Number 79759 to the extent embraced by Katibayan ', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '1st', '2010-10-03', '0523-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends approval of the above stated proposed resolution. (CR NR. 0523-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved; Res-162-2010 (16 Aug 2010, 5)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon; Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation, 3rd Ind., 06 Jul 2010;', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(45, '2010-08-03', '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0054-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Calling for the privatization of the Asin Hydroelectric Power Plants, reiterating the request to submit the Terms of Reference within fifteen (15) days from approval of this resolution and', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-08-03', 'Approved as amended (8 Mar 2010, 55a)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
