(56, '2010-10-03', '09:55:00', '-none-', 'Notice of Hearing', 'Ms. Grace V. Manuel, Officer-in-Charge, Commission Secretariat, National Telecommunications Commission, Quezon City', 'Notice of Hearing dated 25 February 2010 issued by Ms. Grace V. Manuel, Officer-in-Charge, Commission Secretariat, National Telecommunications Commission, Quezon City, regarding the following requests on the application of First United Broadcasting Corpor', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '1st', '2010-12-03', '00341-10', 'Applicant, First United Broadcasting Corporation, a domestic corporation duly organized and existing under Philippine laws was granted a congressional franchise to operate UHF Television Communication System by virtue of Republic Act No. 8699. The hearing was scheduled March 22, 2010 and presumably the Notice of Hearing was published pursuant to existing laws.\r\n         With the scheduled hearing having been lapsed, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to have the matter be NOTED for being moot and academic. (CR NR. 00341-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED for being moot and academic (17 May 2010, 43)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(57, '2010-10-03', '10:45:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0025-10 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as ?Establishing the Public Information and Education Campaign (PIEC) of the City Government of Baguio through the creation of the PIEC Council.?', '-none-', '(NOTE:  [a] FIRST READING -15 March 2010 (Item 17, 23 August 2010 Agenda)\r\n             [b]      SECOND READING AND FOR PUBLICATION BY POSTING ? 27 September 2010\r\n                -  Posted in the  bulletin boards of the City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library  and the Health Services Office starting 28 September 2010.)', 'Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel', '1st', NULL, '0903-10', 'The Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel recommends that the proposed ordinance be APPROVED on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION BY POSTING.\r\n            Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez, Member of the Committee, signified ?Subject to availability of funds.?\r\n            Hon. Edison R. Bilog, Member of the Committee, signified ?The amount should first be determined and then the certification for funding should be secured.?\r\n (CR NR. 0903-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Deferred - returned to the Committee for further study with the information that the above proposed ordinance was forwarded to the Local Finance Committee for issuance of a certification of availability of funds; Forwarded to the Local Finance Committee thru Atty. Leticia O. Clemente, Chairperson, Baguio City, for issuance of a certification of availability of funds (24 Jan 2011, 19)', '7th', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(58, '2010-10-03', '10:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Aurelio D. Placido, President, Pico, Puguis, Longlong, Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (PPLMJODA)', 'Letter dated 09 March 2010 of Mr. Aurelio D. Placido, President, Pico, Puguis, Longlong, Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (PPLMJODA) to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, requesting that their association be included in the agenda for d', '-none-', '(NOTE: [a] Related matters were returned to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation on 05 March 2010.\r\n[b] Sangguniang Bayan Resolution 1-2010, of La Trinidad, Benguet, entitled ?Favorably endorsing the herein request of the La Trinidad Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (LATJODA) and Pico, Puguis, Longlong, Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (PPLMJODA), to the Honorable Sangguniang Panlungsod of Baguio City for its favorable consideration.?)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '6th', '2010-08-07', '0453-10', 'With the foregoing reasons stated in its 2nd Indorsement dated 17 May 2010, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to APPROVE that the BUHAGAN ROAD (formerly Bokawkan Road) be OPENED for the public utility jitneys associations with more than twenty units and observing the ?odd-even scheme?:\r\n           Further recommending to APPROVE that all public utility buses and vans-for-hire parked under a contract of lease or agreement with the Dangwa Terminal Compound or its leasing company be relocated to the Slaughter Terminal, Sto. Ni?o Barangay and only public utility jitneys be allowed to park and load/unload at the Dangwa Terminal Compound.\r\n           Recommending finally to APPROVE that all structures or shanties built at the Tabora Park area be demolished and prohibit any person from installing any structure or shanty for the purpose of trade, business or quarters.  The Tabora Park shall be converted as a staging area for all other public utility jitneys not accommodated at the Dangwa Terminal Compound. (CR NR. 0453-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation; Deferred (28 Jun 2010, 5c2)', '6th', '2010-08-07', 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the same committee, 2nd Ind, 12 Mar 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
