(102, NULL, '09:18:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr.', '1st Indorsement dated 22 April 2010 of then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., returning the unsigned Resolution Numbered 388, series of 2009, entitled ?Resolving to allot a separate electric meter to the Registry of Deeds, Land Registration Authority-C', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above resolution was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on 22 October 2009 and was returned unsigned to the Office of the City Secretary on 27 April 2010.)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', NULL, '00474-10', 'A resolution is a format or written expression of opinion, sentiment, or intention. It is also the act of determining what action or course of action to be done. There are also non-binding resolutions, which are measures that do not become laws.\r\n       The City Mayor returned the above mentioned resolutions unsigned but with comments, which is neither an approval nor a veto. His intention is not known whether he agrees or disagrees with the City Council?s expression of opinions or sentiments.\r\n        Wherefore, considering that a resolution is an expression of a sentiment, opinion or intention, the Committee on Laws shall treat the unsigned city Council Resolutions effective for all legal intents and purposes. \r\n      Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez, Member of the Committee, signified ?For discussion en banc please?. (CR NR. 00474-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 61d)', '4th', '2010-07-07', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(103, NULL, '09:18:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr.', '1st Indorsement dated 22 April 2010 of then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., returning the unsigned Ordinance Numbered 20, series of 2010, entitled ?Realigning the amount of P175,000.00 under Item No. 106 (Barangay Development Programs) of the 2007 An', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above ordinance was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on 20 April 2010  and was returned unsigned to the Office of the City Secretary on 27 April 2010.)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', NULL, '0450-10', 'The City Mayor?s Office returned the above stated matter, inviting the attention of the City Council Members to the Omnibus Election Code (BP 881) particularly:\r\n     1. Art. XXII, Sec. 261 (a) (1) and (2) ?Vote buying and Vote Selling?; and\r\n     2. Art. XXII, Sec. 261 (v) ?Prohibition against release, disbursement and expenditure of public funds.? \r\nThe Committee on Laws finds that the above cited sections of the Omnibus Election Code are NOT APPLICABLE to Ordinance Numbered 20, series of 2010, for the following reasons:\r\n     a) The intention of the ordinance is to construct additional classrooms which should not be construed as vote buying or vote selling;\r\n     b) As cited by COMELEC Resolution No. 8732, Section 261 of the Omnibus Election Code, the prohibited acts refers only to RELEASE, DISBURSEMENT, or EXPENDITURE OF PUBLIC FUNDS effective March 26 ? May 10, 2010, realignment therefore is not a prohibited act.\r\nBasic is the principle that, ?What the law does not include, it excludes.?\r\n     c) The project has yet to be bidded out and therefore no public funds were disbursed.\r\n           Wherefore, the Committee on Laws recommends to override the veto of Ordinance Numbered 20, series of 2010. (CR NR. 0450-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation; Deferred (28 Jun 2010, 49)', '4th', '2010-07-07', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
