(141, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Kagawad Ofelia Estrada', 'Letter dated 13 April 2010 of Kagawad Ofelia Estrada, Committee-Chairman on Market and Public Utilities of AZKCO Barangay ?requesting for the approval to conduct a livelihood project for the barangay through a trade fair to be held at Igorot Park on April', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '00354-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends DENIAL based on the following:\r\n1.	No fund-raising activity may be held within sixty (60) days prior to or after an election Pursuant to Art. 101, paragraph a, number 11, of the Local Government Code, to wit:\r\n           Hold fund-raising activities for barangay projects without the need of securing permits from any national or local office or agency. The proceeds from such activities shall be tax-exempt and shall accrue to the general fund of the barangay provided that in the appropriation thereof, the specific purpose for which such fund-raising activity has been held shall be first satisfied and provided further, that no fund-raising activities shall be held within a period of sixty (60) days immediately preceding and after a national or local election, recall, referendum, or plebiscite (underscoring ours).\r\n2.	The CEPMO is denying the request, pursuant to Sec. 2 of CO No. 10, series of 2008, to wit:\r\n                 It is hereby declared a policy of the Local Government of Baguio City to regulate trade fairs in the City of Baguio by allowing the conduct of trade fairs for a period of not exceeding 15 days in suitable public or private places, except in Burnham Park, the People?s Park, and other city-owned or city-managed public parks within the Central Business District, that promote agricultural, industrial, indigenous and commercial products, crafts, and other merchandise through inter-regional trading that will foster better livelihood opportunities, enhance local tourism, and help advance economic development. \r\n        Hon. Richard A. Cari?o, Member of the Committee, signified ?for discussion?. (CR NR. 00354-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws with the information that the above matters were noted during the 17 May 2010 Regular Session and for the committee to come up with a clearer report (17 May 2010, 56b)', '3rd', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(142, '2010-12-05', '02:00:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Local Finance Committee', '3rd Indorsement dated 19 April 2010 of the Local Finance Committee, returning the Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0032-10 of then City Councilor Galo D. Weygan, informing among others that a supplemental budget goes through the same process as with the preparat', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO  0032-10 of Hon. Galo D. Weygan ?Appropriating the sum of One Hundred Million Pesos (P 100,000,000.00) supplemental budget for various development projects?, which was forwarded to the Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster A, on 06 April 2010.)', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster A: Budget, Appropriations and Expenditures)', '4th', NULL, '0446-10', 'The Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster A, recommends that the above proposed ordinance be returned to the proponent in view of the comments of the Local Finance Committee as contained in the 3rd Indorsement dated 19 April 2010. (CR NR. 0446-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'returned to the proponent, Hon. Galo D. Weygan, SP Member II, in view of the comments of the Local Finance Committee as contained in the 3rd Indorsement dated 19 April 2010 (21 Jun 2010, 90b)', '6th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
