(173, NULL, '10:15:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 007-08 of Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Providing free movie passes for senior citizens in all movie houses of their choice operating within the City of Baguio.?', 'PO 007-08', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 073-09 of Hon. Betty Lourdes F. Tabanda and Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Requesting SM Cinema to grant free movie admission for senior citizens on Mondays?  which was forwarded to the Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor)\r\n(NOTE: [a] The above proposed ordinance was published in the Baguio Reporter issue of 24 February 2008 and was also posted in the bulletin boards of the City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library and the Health Services Office starting 15 February 2008; and [b] The following personalities were invited in today\'s meeting to clarify some issues relative to the above proposal: a) Ms. Annaliza Ramos/Mr. Warly Ybanez, Theater Managers, SM City Baguio; b) Ms. Amelia Brondo, Cinema Manager, Baguio Centermall; c) Dr. Lily Sunga, cinema Manager, Empire Cinema; d) Prof. Federico A. Balanag, president/CEO, Baguio Association of Retired Persons Foundation, Inc. (BFI); e) Mr. Ernesto C. Esguerra, Chairperson, Office of the Senior Citizens Affairs (OSCA), Office of the City Social Welfare and Development Officer, Baguio City; and f) Engr. Leopoldo S. Esca?o, President, Federation of Baguio Senior citizens Association (FBASECA), Senior Citizens Center.', 'Committee on Social Services, Women and Urban Poor', '1st', NULL, '359-09', 'While in its 4th Indorsement dated 27 May 2008, the Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor recommended approval on Second Reading after Publication as per discussions in the Council Session of July 7, 2008, the committee was instructed to consult with movie house operators regarding the proposal.\r\n            Both SM and Baguio Center Mall interpose no objection to the benevolent intent of the proposed ordinance. However, they both state that the movie industry business is not a very profitable one at this time. As Mr. Johan Teope of Baguio Center Mall states:\r\n                   ?As private enterprises that have invested a considerable amount to a profit making venture, we aim, at the very least, to recover our investment within a reasonable period of time and generate some income from the within a reasonable period of time and generate some income from the business to be able to sustain operations. Both objectives, in light of the unabated proliferation of pirated DVDs and the economic downturn, are already difficult to achieve.\r\n        For its part, SM Cinema provides free movies for senior citizens on the first screening every Tuesday. A commitment has also been made for Mondays. They find this proposal ?as an addition to our already heavy burden of trying to keep our business afloat?.\r\n        Instead, both are suggesting that the city should come up with a well thought out incentive scheme that will prove to be attractive for all concerned.\r\n        In view of the above, this committee recommends that the proposed ordinance be returned to the proponent to consider the proposal of the movie house operators. (CR NR. 359-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Back to proponent to consider the proposal of the movie house operators', '7th', NULL, 'Acted Upon', 'FLB 2009', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
