(209, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Vetoed', 'Unsigned Ordinance', '1st Indorsement dated 16 July 2007 of then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. returning the unsigned Ordinance Numbered 26, series of 2007, entitled ?Promulgating the use of paper bags, buri bags and other biodegradable bagging containers in all supermar', 'Unsigned Ordinance No. 26-07', '(NOTE:  The above ordinance was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on 05 July 2007 and was returned unsigned to the Office of the Acting City Secretary on 18 July 2007.)\r\n(NOTE: The Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 104-08 of Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan, Jr. ?Providing for the use of paper bags and boxes, buri bags and other biodegradable bagging containers, wrapping and packaging materials in all supermarkets, groceries and retail business establishments including food processors/manufacturers in the City of Baguio? was returned to the Committee on Laws on November 2008 for consolidation with the returned unsigned Ordinance Numbered 26, series of 2007.)', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons.', '3rd', '2008-10-11', '094-09', 'The ordinance was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on July 5, 2007 and was returned unsigned to the Office of the Acting City Secretary on July 18, 2007, a period of thirteen (13) days. If the intention of returning the ordinance unsigned is to veto it, the veto must be communicated by the Local Chief Executive to the Sangguniang Panlungsod within ten (10) days; otherwise, the ordinance shall be deemed approved as if he had signed it.\r\n         The Committee on Laws therefore recommends that the above matter be NOTED, considering that Ordinance Numbered 26, series of 2007 is deemed approved and effective due to the inaction of the City Mayor to approve or veto the ordinance within a period of ten (10) days as provided for by law. (CR NR. 094-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted Upon', 'Research', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
