(264, NULL, '08:45:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. Nicasio S. Palaganas', '1st Indorsement dated 17 May 2010 of Hon. Nicasio S. Palaganas, suggesting that any person/s mentioned in the undated handwritten petition of concerned residents of Slaughterhouse Compound Barangay, Baguio City, regarding the illegal bingo game in the sai', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to  undated handwritten petition of concerned residents of Slaughterhouse Compound Barangay, Baguio City, to Hon. Richard A. Cari?o, requesting assistance for the immediate demolition of the illegal bingo game in their barangay, which was forwarded to the Committee on Human Rights, Justice, Public Protection and Safety, Peace and Order on 17 May 2010.)', 'Committee on Human Rights, Justice, Public Protection and Safety, Peace and Order for information', '2nd', NULL, '0573-10', 'The Committee on Human Rights, Justice, Public Protection and Safety, Peace and Order recommends that the aforementioned communication be NOTED on the following grounds, to wit:\r\n     1. The proposal to invite persons named in the handwritten petition is not advisable considering that the letter speaks of unidentified persons. Although it speaks of one ?Deligero? and ?Barangay Officials?, we cannot identify in particularity who the petitioners are referring to. To invite all persons with a name ?Deligero? and all the ?Barangay Officials? of Sto. Ni?o Barangay would be unfair to those persons who are not in any way involved in this case. Further, to invite all ?Deligero? and ?Barangay Officials? would like be a fishing expedition on the part of the City Council.\r\n     2. The City Mayor has already acted on the matter when Hon. Philian Louise C. Weygan called the attention of the City Mayor in an Executive and Legislative meeting.\r\n     3. The Barangay Captain concerned had written the City Legal  Officer informing the latter that as per MOA signed by the operator and the barangay council, the fund raising would last only until July 31, 2010. Thus upon approval of this committee report the issue would be MOOT and ACADEMIC.\r\n (CR NR. 0573-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-02-08', 'returned to the Committee for further study (02 Aug 2010, 39a)', '6th', '2010-04-08', '; Forwarded to the Committee on Human rights, Justice, Public Protection and Safety, Peace and Order for study and recommendation, 4th Ind., 07 Jul 2010;', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(265, NULL, '04:27:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Antonio L. Tabin, City Accountant', 'Letter dated 26 May 2010 of Mr. Antonio L. Tabin, City Accountant, requesting hiring of four (4) casual Administrative Assistant II, SG-8, for the period July 1, 2010 to December 31, 2010.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel', '1st', NULL, '0424-10', 'The Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel recommends APPROVAL of the herein request of Mr. Antonio L. Tabin, City Accountant, for the hiring of services of four (4) casual Administrative Assistant II, SG-8, for the period July 1, 2010 to December 31, 2010 provided that the salaries and other emoluments of the said casual employees shall be charged against the 2010 Annual Budget appropriations for personnel services of the said office; and providing further that the said office shall start processing the filling up of the said casual positions into permanent Plantilla positions. (CR NR. 0424-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-07-06', 'Approved (7 Jun 2010, 99b)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(266, NULL, '11:17:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'Country Club Village Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 11, series of 2010, of Country Club Village Barangay, entitled ?A resolution of the Sangguniang Barangay changing the title of the calamity project ?restoration of eroded pathway at Sector G? to ?repair and rehabilitation of pathwa', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Works', '1st', NULL, '0464-10', 'The Committee on Public Works recommends that the above be reverted to the General Fund and the same be reappropriated.\r\nThe committee further recommends APPROVAL of the above matter and be converted into an ordinance [Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0052-10] and be approved dispensing with the readings. (CR NR. 0464-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (21 Jun 2010, 108)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(267, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr.', 'Implementation of Republic Act No. 10023 and DENR Administative Order No. 2010-12 in the City of Baguio.\r\n\r\nProposed Resolution Nr. PR 077-10 of Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr. ?Inviting the Regional Executive Director of the Department of Environment and Nat', '-none-', '(NOTE: [a] The above matter is related to the Memorandum dated 14 October 2010 issued by Dir. Clarence L. Baguilat, CESO III, Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR-CAR to the Director, Lands Management Bureau, re: request of the Regional Executive Director, DENR-CAR, for clarification on the implementation of Republic Act No. 10023 in the City of Baguio and forwarding the proposed guidelines drafted by the DENR-CAR for his review, evaluation and consideration. This was forwarded to the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing on 27 October 2010 for information.\r\n[b] Resolution Numbered 122, s. 2010 requested the DENR-CAR to hold in abeyance the implementation of R.A. No. 10023 or the Residential Free Patent Law pending approval of the specific guidelines of R.A. 10023 for the City of Baguio.)\r\n\r\n\r\n(NOTE:  a.  Republic Ac t No. 10023, entitled ?An act authorizing the issuance of free patents to residential lands?; and\r\n        b.  DENR Administrative Order No. 2010-12, entitled ?Rules and regulations for the issuance of free patents to residential lands under Republic Act No. 10023.?)', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '1st', NULL, '1008-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends the following:\r\n     1. That a committee be created through the issuance of an administrative order by the Office of the City Mayor, Baguio City to review, study and recommend  appropriate  action on the above Administrative Order No. 2010-12 and the Draft Administrative Order ?Providing guidelines for the disposition of alienable and disposable public lands suitable for residential purposes in the City of Baguio relative to Republic Act No. 10023 ?An act authorizing the issuance of free patents to residential lands?.?\r\n     2. That the committee be composed of the City Mayor as Chairman, City Legal Officer as Co-Chairman and the Chairman of the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing, the City Planning and Development Coordinator, the City Assessor and representatives from the DENR-CAR, HLURB-CAR, and Registry of Deeds as members, without prejudice of appointing other members as the need arises.\r\n     3. To reiterate the request of the city to DENR-CAR Regional Executive Director Clarence L. Baguilat, to hold in abeyance the implementation of Republic Act No. 10023 and Administrative Order No. 2010-12 until such time that specific guidelines for its implementation for the City of Baguio be prepared and jointly approved by DENR and the City Government of Baguio. (CR NR. 1008-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved; Res-029-2011 (31 Jan 2011, 36)', '1st', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
