(278, NULL, '11:30:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Annual Budget for CY 2010', 'Engineer?s Hill Barangay', 'Annual Budget of Engineer?s Hill Barangay for CY 2010 amounting to P1,951,855.00.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster C: Review of Barangay Budgets and Barangay Tax Ordinances; Acrreditation of NGOs and other concerns)', '1st', '2010-06-07', '0530-10', 'The Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster C, recommends FAVORABLE REVIEW of the above mentioned Barangay Budgets and that the same be returned to the concerned barangays through the City Budget Officer for implementation. Further, that the City Budget Officer, thru a copy of the resolution, coordinate with the appropriate offices with the end in view of having the barangays submit budget ordinances in the appropriate and standard format. (CR NR. 0530-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (26 Jul 2010, 15c)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(279, NULL, '05:20:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Gerardo P. Verzosa, General Manager, BENECO', 'Letter dated 28 June 2010 of Mr. Gerardo P. Verzosa, General Manager, BENECO, informing the City Council that BENECO will be filing its Application for the Approval of Capital Expenditures for the Year 2010 to 2012 in compliance with the Energy Regulatory', '-none-', '(NOTE: [a] ERC Resolution No. 26, series of 2009 amended the rules for approval of regulated entities capital expenditure projects?;\r\n[b] The following personalities were requested to be present in today?s meeting:\r\n      1.  President and Members of the Board of Directors, BENECO, to clarify matters relative to the application of BENECO for the approval of Capital Expenditures Projects for the year 2010 to 2012 in compliance with the ERC Resolution No. 26, series of 2009, matters relative to the Power Purchase Adjustment (PPA), and the purchase of 1.2 hectare property located at South Drive, Baguio City;\r\n(NOTE:  The Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0056-10 of Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Inviting the President and Members of the Board of Directors of Benguet Electric Cooperative (BENECO) to clarify matters pertaining to the purchase of the 1.2 hectare lot along South Drive, Baguio City and to submit pertinent documents regarding said purchase like, but not limited to, Deed of Absolute Sale, BIR payments, receipt of payment, escrow agreement, sworn statement from the authorized representative of the regulating entity and  others to the City Council in aid of legislation? was forwarded to Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation on 19 March 2010.)\r\n\r\n2.  Engr. Evelyn B. Cayat, Officer-in-Charge, City Planning and Development Office, to clarify matters whether or not the construction of a facility sub-station on the purchased lot of BENECO along South Drive, Baguio City, is within the zoning plan of the City of Baguio; and\r\n     \r\n     3.   Dir. Clarence L. Baguilat, CESO III, Regional Executive Director, DENR-CAR, to shed light on the alleged tree cutting activity on the purchased lot of BENECO along South Drive, Baguio City.)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '1st', '2010-06-07', '0510-10', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends APPROVAL of the letter request of BENECO to post in the bulletin board of the City Hall its application for the approval of the Capital Expenditures for the year 2010 to 2012 in compliance with ERC Resolution No. 26 and for the issuance of a certification bearing the dry seal of the City Council as proof of posting. \r\n        Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen, Member of the Committee, signified ?suggest invite members of the board to ask if CAPEX will result in increase of electrical rate.? (CR NR. 0510-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-06-09', 'LOST (06 Sep 2010, 2)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(280, NULL, '01:33:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Rafael C. Valencia, President & Operations Manager, 911 on Call Incorporated, BGH Compound, Baguio City', 'Letter dated 15 June 2010 of Mr. Rafael C. Valencia, President & Operations Manager, 911 on Call Incorporated, BGH Compound, Baguio City, submitting their intention for the renewal of accreditation to the Local Special Bodies under the City?s Development ', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster C: Review of Barangay Budgets and Barangay Tax Ordinances; Acrreditation of NGOs and other concerns)', '1st', '2010-06-07', '0569-10', 'After review of the supporting documents which show compliance with the requirements of law as provided for by the provisions of the Local Government Code of 1991, its implementing Rules and Regulations and pertinent Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) Memorandum Circulars, the Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster C, recommends APPROVAL of the foregoing request for accreditation, provided that the organization submits to the Sangguniang Panlungsod their annual accomplishment reports and financial statements on or before the 20th day of January of every year thereafter, and their membership in local special body shall be co-terminus with that of the Local Chief Executive. (CR NR. 0569-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-02-08', 'Approved; Res 156, s 2010 (02 Aug 2010, 35)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
