(320, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Daniel T. Farinas', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PO 094-05 of Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as \"Proposing that the boundary between Scout Barrio Barangay and Country Club Village Barangay be amended to conform with the present situation affecting them.\"', '094-05', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', NULL, '0418-12', 'Having been overtaken by events, particularly the conduct of the POLITICAL BOUNDARY SURVEY PROJECT, CAD 1216-d BAGUIO CITY CADASTRE by the DENR-CAR, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above matters BE FORWARDED to the Office of the Regional Technical Director, Lands Management Services, DENR-CAR, Diego Silang St., Baguio City, for appropriate information and consideration. The said political boundary survey has already been completed and submitted by the contractor to the DENR-CAR. (CR NR. 0418-12); The Committee on Barangay Affairs recommends that the matter be forwarded to the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing, Office of Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., for their consideration and guidance in conducting the determination of the political boundaries of the 128 barangays of Baguio City. (CR NR. 0383-12); The Committee on Barangay Affairs recommends that the Proposed Ordinance Nr. 094-05 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as ?Proposing that the boundary between Scout Barrio Barangay and Country Club Village Barangay be amended to conform with the present situation affecting them? be approved on THIRD and FINAL READING. (CR NR. 0049-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2012-06-08', 'forwarded to Atty. Crizaldy M. Barcelo, CESO III, Regional Techinical Director, Lands Management Services, DENR-CAR, Diego Silang St., Baguio City, for appropriate information and consideration. The said political boundary survey has already been completed and submitted by the contractor to the DENR-CAR. It is further suggested that the manifestation of Hon. Nicasio S. Palaganas during the 06 august 2012 Regular Session be considered (06 Aug 2012, 49a); forwarded to the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing, Sangguniang Panlungosd, for consideration and guidance in conducting the determination of the political boundaries of the 128 barangays in Baguio City, per recommendation of the Committee on Barangay Affairs, approved during the 23 July 2012 Regular Session (23 Jul 2012, 37a); Returned to the Committee for further study and for the committee to set a dialouge between the two (2) barangays as manifested during the 01 March 2010 Regular Session (1 Mar 2010, 58a)', '9th', '2012-08-08', 'Acted upon; [Formerly indorsed to the Committee on Barangay Affairs, 1st Ind. September 13, 2005]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(321, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Leandro B. YangotJr.', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 192-05 of then City Councilor Leandro B. Yangot Jr. \"Requesting her Excellency, President Gloria Macapagal-Arroyo to set aside by way of a Presidential Proclamation the public land covering the area where the Mabini Elementary S', '192-05', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '1st', '2005-05-09', '112-09', 'Subject of the above matters are two (2) parcels of land identified as Lot 96-A and Lot 97-B containing an area of 6,935 square meters and 14,355 square  meters, respectively, located along Leonard Wood Road and Happy Glen Loop Road, Baguio City. The same were identified as Government Center Elementary School under the City of Baguio, now the Mabini Elementary School, by Bsd-20561 surveyed in 1955 and approved by the Director of Lands on April 20, 1955.\r\n          In view thereof, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends APPROVAL of the above resolution with the following amendments:\r\n1.	That the subject area for proclamation shall be 21,290 square meters, covering Lots 96-A and 97-B of Bsd-20561;\r\n2.	That the proclamation be in the name of the City of Baguio and the Mabini Elementary School.\r\n         Likewise, the committee adopts to be the author in view of the fact that the proponent is no longer a member of the City Council. (CR NR. 112-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Res 047-09', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted Upon', 'Research', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
