(384, NULL, '02:05:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Raquel Quiteves', 'Letter dated 21 September 2005 of Ms. Raquel Quiteves and Ms. Cecilia Centeno, seeking assistance on their application to lease stalls beneath the stairs of the Fish Section of the Carinderia Building at the Baguio City Market.', 'Fish Section', '-none-', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '2nd', NULL, '0544-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends that the letters as found in (a) and (b) above BE NOTED for the following reasons:\r\n1. The requested area is an unloading area for bulk fish deliveries (?bagsakan?) and a common passageway for vendors and buyers.  To award this space would result to constriction of the area causing pedestrian traffic, lack of ?bagsakan? area and endanger market goers in case of emergencies;\r\n2.A similar request made by Shirley Aquino, represented by Mr. Ilalo Cardinal was recommended to be NOTED, after the Sangguniang Panlungsod failed to override it.  Thereby, there is equal application of the law to all applicants covering the subject area. (CR NR. 0544-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (26 Jul 2010, 29)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(385, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Peter L. Sagayo, President, Baguio Market Vendor\'s Association and Mr. Pablo C. Agulto, Chairman, Baguio Market Multi-Purpose Cooperative,', 'Letter dated 20 September 2005 of Mr. Peter L. Sagayo, President, Baguio Market Vendor\'s Association and Mr. Pablo C. Agulto, Chairman, Baguio Market Multi-Purpose Cooperative, appelaing to the Honorable City Council to consider their request for an exemp', 'Business Taxes', '(NOTE:The 1st Indorsement dated 03 August 2005 of ms. Thelma B. Manaois, City TYreasurer, requesting appropriate action on the unpaid rental of the BAMARVA and BAMARVEMPCO to the city for that area where their building is erected at the Baguio City Market in the amount of P9,520.00 montly effective August 2003 was forwarded to the Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce on 07 September 2005.)', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '2nd', NULL, '0639-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends to FORWARD the above requests to the City Treasurer?s Office for comment/s and/or recommendation/s.\r\n            BAMARVA has been DISSOLVED as a corporation when its corporate term expired on September 20, 2005. Since 2009, BAMARVACO has occupied the building previously occupied by BAMARVA.\r\n            The City Treasurer is requested to submit an assessment of the liabilities on unpaid rental of BAMARVA and BAMARVACO, if any.\r\n            Lastly, the City Treasurer is requested to submit a report containing her findings on whether or not the subject building is being used solely as an office of BAMARVACO of if commercial spaces are being leased out. (CR NR. 0639-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-09-08', 'FORWARDED to the City Treasurer\'s Office thru Ms. Thelma B. Manaois, City Treasurer, Baguio City, for comment/s and/or recommendation/s. The City Treasurer is requested to submit an assessment of the liabilities on unpaid rental of BAMARVA and BAMARVACO, if any and a report containing her findings on whether or not the subject building is being used solely as an office of BAMARVACO or if commercial spaces are being leased out (09 Aug 2010, 76b)', '6th', '2010-11-08', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(386, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'egitimate stall holders and members of the Fish Section Association', 'Letter dated 26 September 2005 of the legitimate stallholders and members of the Fish Section Association, Carinderia Building, Baguio City Market, strongly protesting the approval by the Sangguninag Panlungsod the Committee Report Nr. 05-698 approving th', 'Fish Section', '(NOTE: The request of Ms. Shirley Aquino for the use of the space located at the Carinderia Building beneath the stairs at the Baguio City Market Fish Section was approved  during the 19 September 2005 Regular Session.)', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '1st', NULL, '0546-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends that the above letters be NOTED for the following reasons:\r\n1. Resolution Nr. 261-2005, which earlier approved the space applied for by Ms. Shirley Aquino, was VETOED by then Hon. City Mayor Braulio D. Yaranon.  The Sangguniang Panlungsod failed to muster enough affirmative votes to override the veto;\r\n2. As previously stated, the space being applied for is an unloading area for bulk fish deliveries (?bagsakan?) and a passageway of vendors and buyers.  To award the area will result to pedestrian congestion, reduction or eradication of the ?bagsakan? area and may endanger the market goers in case of an emergency;\r\n3. There are available stalls at the interior section of the Fish Market which can be applied for;\r\n4. There exists an opposition from the legitimate stall holders and members of the Fish Section Association, which supports the maintenance of the area free from any obstructions to fully serve its intended purposes as passageway and ?bagsakan? area.\r\n\r\n(NOTE:  In the 2nd Indorsement dated 23 March 2009 of then Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista, Jr., His Honor returned City Council Resolution Numbered 058, series of 2009  [Forwarding to the Office of the City Mayor the Appeal for Reconsideration of Mr. Ilalo Cardinal on the Denial by the Baguio City Market Authority (BCMA) of his application for the use of the ?Bagsakan Area? at the Baguio City Public Market?], Denying with Finality, the appeal of Mr. Ilalo Cardinal and other applications for the use of the bagsakan area at the Baguio City Public Market, pursuant to Resolution Numbered 010-08 and item no. 4 of the main agenda of the minutes of the meeting on 06 March 2009 of the Baguio City Market Authority.) (CR NR. 0546-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (26 Jul 2010, 31a)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(387, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Engr. Nazita F. Ba?ez', 'Letter dated 7 September 2005 of Engr. Nazita F. Ba?ez, OIC-Assistant Department Head and Action Officer on Waste Management, noted by Arch. Josephine B. Chan, OIC Department Head, CEPMO, forwarding documents relative to the project of the city, entitled ', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons', '1st', '2005-08-09', '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Refer to Committee', '-none-', NULL, 'Invitations were sent to the City Budget Officer, Engr. Nazita Ba?ez and Ms. Evelyn Lorenzo, Office of the City Mayor to shed light on matters relevant to the Irisan Open Dumpsite Project on 24 October 2005 and 07 November 2005 Regular Session.', 'Solid Waste Management', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
