(605, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'commuters and residents of Virac, Itogon, Benguet', 'Letter dated 12 November 2009 of the commuters and residents of Virac, Itogon, Benguet seeking help to address the jeepneys transportation problem in their locality and requesting to designate additional jeepneys units.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '4th', '2010-07-07', '0458-10', 'Primordial consideration in the grant of a certificate of convenience is the interest and welfare of the riding public.  The grant of a franchise to an applicant is espoused by the objective of public service.  Other pertinent and important requirements are technical in nature and left to the discretion of the approving office like the LTFRB and City Council.\r\n            In order that the welfare of the residents and commuters of Bubon, Virac, Itogon, Benguet be given action, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the herein listed applicants for the issuance of new franchises be EXEMPTED from the application of LTFRB MC No. 96-002 provided that their parking/loading area shall not be within the Central Business District. (CR NR. 0458-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwrded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 52c)', '4th', '2010-07-07', 'Pending; [Foremerly indorsed and referred to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(606, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'commuters and passengers of Bubon, Virac, Itogon', 'Letter dated 04 January 2010 of the commuters and passengers of Bubon, Virac, Itogon to Atty. Federico J. Mandapat Jr., Regional Director, DOTC-CAR, bringing to the Regional Director?s attention their need of additional passenger jeepneys due to limited p', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '4th', '2010-07-07', '0458-10', 'Primordial consideration in the grant of a certificate of convenience is the interest and welfare of the riding public.  The grant of a franchise to an applicant is espoused by the objective of public service.  Other pertinent and important requirements are technical in nature and left to the discretion of the approving office like the LTFRB and City Council.\r\n            In order that the welfare of the residents and commuters of Bubon, Virac, Itogon, Benguet be given action, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the herein listed applicants for the issuance of new franchises be EXEMPTED from the application of LTFRB MC No. 96-002 provided that their parking/loading area shall not be within the Central Business District. (CR NR. 0458-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 52d)', '4th', '2010-07-07', 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(607, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'SOFAD Resolution', 'Sangguniang Bayan of Itogon, Benguet', 'SOFAD Resolution No. 328, series of 2009, of the Sangguniang Bayan of Itogon, Benguet  ?Forwarding the letter of Virac-Bubon commuters to the Office of the LTFRB-CAR through the Regional Director, Atty. Federico J. Mandapat Jr.?', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '4th', '2010-07-07', '0458-10', 'Primordial consideration in the grant of a certificate of convenience is the interest and welfare of the riding public.  The grant of a franchise to an applicant is espoused by the objective of public service.  Other pertinent and important requirements are technical in nature and left to the discretion of the approving office like the LTFRB and City Council.\r\n            In order that the welfare of the residents and commuters of Bubon, Virac, Itogon, Benguet be given action, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the herein listed applicants for the issuance of new franchises be EXEMPTED from the application of LTFRB MC No. 96-002 provided that their parking/loading area shall not be within the Central Business District. (CR NR. 0458-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 52e)', '4th', '2010-07-07', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(608, NULL, '09:30:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Consuelo D. Manansala, Office of the Executive Vice President, Operations Sector, GSIS', 'Letter dated 31 of Ms. Consuelo D. Manansala, Office of the Executive Vice President, Operations Sector, GSIS, reiterating the reply of their GSIS Baguio Branch Office, on Resolution Nr. 94, Series of 2010, with the information that as of 21 May 2010, upo', '-none-', '[NOTE: The same letter was furnished to the Honorable Members on June 02, 2010 and the    following were furnished to the Honorable Members:\r\n        a]   Letter dated 25 May 2010 of Ms. Nora M. Saludares, Senior Vice President, GSIS to Ms. Maria Remedios Agranzamendez, Local Legislative Staff Officer V, City Council, Baguio City, informing her that the matter regarding Resolution No. 094-2010 was referred to their Operations Sector, for information and appropriate action.\r\nb.] Letter dated 24 May 2010 of Ms. Veronica Victorina B. Perez, Branch Head, Government Service Insurance System, Baguio Branch Office, to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, informing His Honor that  in line with City Resolution Numbered 094, series of 2010, their office have just finished their massive claims processing not only of their members in Baguio City but also in Benguet and Mt. Province \r\n   c.]   Resolution Nr. 094, Series of 2010, requested the Government Service Insurance System   to immediately release the benefits of retirees of the City of Baguio as soon as possible.]', 'furnished to the Hon. Members & Research Div.', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(609, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 146-04 of Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as ?Recommending the repairs and rehabilitation of all available and existing water reservoirs in the city to be used as reserve water sources and as catch basins during the rainy season.?', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '0461-10', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the above proposal be APPROVED and all available and existing water reservoirs/catch basins in the city be identified. (CR NR. 0461-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (28 Jun 2010, 55)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(610, NULL, '10:10:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0083-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Reiterating the request of senior citizens and differently-abled persons to establish blue lanes along all areas with pedestrian overpasses.?', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '1st', NULL, '0574-10', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends APPROVAL of the said proposed resolution and the same be forwarded to the City Engineering Office for its comments and recommendations. (CR NR. 0574-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-02-08', 'Deferred - returned to the Committee for further study and to consider the suggestion raised by Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez during the 02 August 2010 Regular Session for the conduct of a public hearing (02 Aug 2010, 40)', '3rd', '2010-04-08', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(611, NULL, '10:10:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0084-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Requesting the City Environment and Parks Management Office (CEPMO) to look for another location for a public cemetery, preferably in the Baguio, La Trinidad, Itogon, Sablan, Tuba and Tubl', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '1st', NULL, '0515-10', 'Considering the hereto attached 3rd Indorsement dated 12 July 2010 of Evelyn B. Cayat, OIC, Office of the City Planning and Development Coordinator, Baguio City, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends APPROVAL of the above proposed resolution. (CR NR. 0515-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (19 Jul 2010, 17)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(612, NULL, '10:10:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0085-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Requesting all owners, operators and/or managers of movie houses in the City of Baguio to increase the free movie entrance benefit of senior citizens to two (2) times a week.?', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor', '1st', NULL, '0500-10', 'Resolution No. 183, series of 2009, entitled ?Requests SM Cinema to grant free movie admission for Senior Citizens on Mondays and expressing appreciation to SM Cinema for providing entertainment to the Senior Citizens?, was approved by the City Council for the benefit of the elderly of the City of Baguio.\r\n            In view of the above, the Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor recommends that the above matter be NOTED. (CR NR. 0500-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Returned to the proponent to study the possibility of how certain local government units were able to successfully increase the movie theater benefits to senior citizens (19 July 2010, 4)', '3rd', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(613, NULL, '02:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Charlie Abance, et al., all officers and members of Tuba, Sto. Tomas Operators & Drivers Association (TUSTODA)', 'Letter dated 16 June 2010 of Mr. Charlie Abance, et al., all officers and members of Tuba, Sto. Tomas Operators & Drivers Association (TUSTODA), requesting reconsideration in the implementation of Ordinance No. 08, series of 2010, amending Ordinance No. 3', '-none-', '(NOTE:   a]     Ord. No. 08, s. 2010 amended ordinance Numbered 33, series of 2009.\r\n        b]    Ord. No. 33, s. 2009 declared it unlawful for Public Utility Buses (PUBs) and Jitneys (PUJs), vans for hire including freight trucks and other vehicles of similar nature, such as trucks masquerading as jeeps, to park or to use any portion of Abanao Street, Chanum Street, Governor Pack Road, Harrison Road, Otek Street, and Tabora Park (along Magsaysay Avenue), including any road, street, right-of-way, plaza, park and other public place as terminal parking space or loading and unloading areas for passengers and goods.)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', NULL, '0629-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends that the above stated matter be transmitted to the City Mayor?s Office considering that the City Mayor executes, enforces and implements all applicable laws and ordinances relative to the governance of the city.\r\n         In Resolution Numbered 246, series of 2004 entitled, ?Approving the request of Tuba-Sto. Tomas Operators and Driver?s Association (TUSTODA) to temporarily use a portion of Chugum Street, Baguio City, as their terminal/loading area, subject conditions?, the use of a portion of Chugum Street is clearly temporary in character.\r\n        Furthermore, conditions 1 and 2 of the above stated resolution is openly violated by the association, which are grounds for immediate revocation as stated in condition 4. (CR NR. 0629-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-09-08', 'transmitted to the Office of the City Mayor, Baguio City, considering that the Honorable City Mayor executes, enforces and implements all applicable laws and ordinances relative to the governance of the city. \r\nIn Resolution Numbered 246, series of 2004, entitled \"Approving the request of Tuba-Sto. Tomas Operators and Driver\'s Association (TUSTODA) to temporarily use a portion of Chugum Street, Baguio City, as their terminal/loading area, subject to conditions\", the use of a portion of Chugum Street is clearly temporary in character. \r\nFurthermore, conditions 1 and 2 of the above stated resolution are openly violated by the association, which are grounds for immediate revocation as stated in condition 4 (09 Aug 2010, 68)', '4th', '2010-11-08', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(614, NULL, '08:55:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Dir. Teresita V. Galacgac, Regional Officer/Director II, Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board', 'Letter dated 01 June 2010 of Dir. Teresita V. Galacgac, Regional Officer/Director II, Housing and Land Use Regulatory Board to then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., endorsing the application for alteration of plan of Heaven?s Garden Memorial Park loca', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Res. Nr. 282, s. 1996 approved the final development of the Heaven?s Garden Memorial Park subject to the conditions set by the Sangguniang Panlungsod (City Council) Committee on Housing and Relocation sites and Lands as contained in its 4th Indorsement dated 29 July 1996.)', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '3rd', NULL, '0705-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends APPROVAL of the above application subject to the following:\r\n1. That the approval is for that parcel of land identified as Phase I, Heaven?s Garden Memorial Park containing an area of 34,636 square meters;\r\n2. That all open spaces including that which is identified as Block 8 shall be maintained as perpetual open spaces;\r\n3. That Phase 1 of Heaven?s Garden Memorial Park shall NOT be eligible for further or future alteration.\r\n              Attached hereto for further information and guidance are the Technical Evaluation from the Office of the City Planning and Development Coordinator dated 13 July 2010 and the letter dated 06 August 2010 of Engr. Marciano L. Garcia submitting additional documents.\r\n (CR NR. 0705-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-08-11', 'Approved; Res-235-2010 (08 Nov 2010, 8)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(615, NULL, '08:55:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Noemi Rillera-Sanchez', 'Letter dated 15 June 2010 of Ms. Noemi Rillera-Sanchez, for and in behalf of the petitioners to Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., submitting their petition opposing the reported plan to convert a portion of Epifanio De Los Santos Street into an alley at Middle', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research', '2nd', NULL, 'EDUC-2017-030', 'The Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research recommends that the matter be NOTED. (EDUC-2017-030).', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2017-06-11', 'NOTED; informed proponent as per the letter dated 07 November 2017 (06 November 2017, 43); cancelled session (30 October 2017).', '-none-', NULL, 'FOR NEXT AGENDA', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(616, NULL, '02:39:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr.', '1st Indorsement dated 15 June 2010 of then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., forwarding for appropriate action the Resolution No. 10-41 of the Municipality of Sablan, Benguet, entitled ?Resolution endorsing the proposed Engineered Sanitary Landfill of ', '-none-', '(NOTE: a]  The same Resolution No. 10-41 of the Municipality of Sablan, Benguet was forwarded to the Committee on Health  on 17 June 2010.\r\n          b] The letter dated 29 March 2010 of Mr. Santiago M. Bartolome, Secretary to the Sanggunian, Sablan, Benguet, transmitting the Sangguniang Bayan Resolution No. 10-30 of Sablan, Benguet, entitled ?Resolution disapproving the request of the City of Baguio for a favorable endorsement of their proposed Engineered Sanitary Landfill to be established in the Municipality of Sablan?, was returned to Mr. Santiago M. Bartolome, Secretary to the Sanggunian, Sablan, Benguet, with the information that during the 17 May 2010 Regular Session, the matter was noted per recommendation of the Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons\r\n           c] The pertinent documents submitted by Mr. Rogelio P. Almacen and Mr. Julius (Butch) J. Mandapat, Atty-in-Fact of Antonia Polon, et al., owners of parcels of land located at Sablan, Benguet Province for possible sanitary landfill  for the City of Baguio.Pertinent documents submitted by Mr. Rogelio P. Almacen and Mr. Julius (Butch) J. Mandapat, Atty-in-Fact of Antonia Polon, et al., owners of parcels of land located at Sablan, Benguet Province for possible sanitary landfill  for the City of Baguio, was forwarded to the Baguio City Solid Waste Maagement Board, thru: Ms. Cordelia M. Lacsamana, OIC, CEPMO, to be consolidated with other presentations on garbage matters which were previously forwarded for comparative analysis as agreed upon during the 23 November 2009 Regular Session of the Sangguniang Panlungsod.)', 'Furnished to the Honorable Members for information', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(617, NULL, '04:45:00', '-none-', 'Position paper', 'Mr. Edward Madongit, President, Baguio-Trinidad Operators and Drivers Association (BTODA), Mr. Avelino Tom, President, Camp Dangwa Operators and Drivers Association (CADODA) and Mr. David Aragon, President , Tomay Greenfields, Incorporated (TGI)', 'Position paper of Mr. Edward Madongit, President, Baguio-Trinidad Operators and Drivers Association (BTODA), Mr. Avelino Tom, President, Camp Dangwa Operators and Drivers Association (CADODA) and Mr. David Aragon, President , Tomay Greenfields, Incorporat', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Related matters were included in the 21 June 2010  Regular Session of the Sangguniang Panlungsod.)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '1st', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(618, NULL, '09:35:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. James Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Jeepney Operators, Drivers Association (LATJODA)', 'Letter dated 16 June 2010of Mr. James Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Jeepney Operators, Drivers Association (LATJODA), stressing that their request is simply a reconsideration of the Hon. City Council to issue a written approval nor any written instrument', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the letter dated 05 April 2010 of Mr. James  J. Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Operators Drivers Association (LATJODA), soliciting consideration of the City Council to issue a written approval to operate ?Off Street Parking? at Shell Abanao and Shell Camp Allen traversing Bokawkan Road. (Item 2b, 21 June 2010 Agenda)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '2nd', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(619, NULL, '08:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Codification Committee', 'Letter dated 12 May 2010 of the Codification Committee on Investment Code and Market Code, submitting a copy of the codified Tax Code which includes the Market Code.', '-none-', '(NOTE: a]   The 1st Indorsement dated 19 May 2008 of Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista, Jr., returning unsigned Ordinance Numbered 35, series of 2008, entitled ?Establishing the Baguio City Investments and Incentives Code (BCIIC)?, for amendment, revision or modification, with the following reasons, among others:\r\n                     ?x x x\r\n                     However, while the Ordinance purports to provide for the establishment of a Baguio City Investments and Incentives Code with the formulation of an Investment Priorities Plan and the registration of enterprises pursuant to such Plan, it practically makes an undue delegation of powers ? both executive and legislative ? to the Baguio City Investment and Incentive Board (BCIIB) and its Investment Promotion Unit (IPU) therein created under Chapters III and IV.\r\n                     x x x.?\r\n                     (NOTE:  The above ordinance was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on 07 May 2008 and was returned to the Office of the Acting City Secretary on 28 May 2008.)\r\n             b]    The Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 035-05 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as ?adopting a codified and comprehensive Market Code in the City of Baguio.?\r\n                    (NOTE: The above cited proposed codified and comprehensive Market Code was posted  in the different sections within the City Public Market, and in the bulletin boards of the City Public Market, City Hall, City Library, Post Office  and the Health Services Office starting 26 October 2005.) (Item 19, 21 November 2005 Agenda)', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Investment Code - referred to the Committee on Laws; Market Code - referred to the Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce (19 Jul 2010, 20)', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(620, NULL, '09:35:00', '-none-', 'Letters', 'Baguio Sabkil Labilab Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (BASLAJODA), Inc. and Baguio Itogon-Sangilo Drivers and Operators Association (BISDOA)', 'a.   Letter dated 16 June 2010 of the Baguio Sabkil Labilab Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (BASLAJODA), Inc., appealing reconsideration that the implementation of City Ordinance No. 08, series of 2010 be held in abeyance and maintain status quo', '-none-', '(NOTE:   a]  Ord. No. 08, s. 2010 amended ordinance Numbered 33, series of 2009;\r\n             b]  Ord. No. 33, s. 2009 declared it unlawful for Public Utility Buses (PUBs) and Jitneys (PUJs), vans for hire including freight trucks and other vehicles of similar nature, such as trucks masquerading as jeeps, to park or to use any portion of Abanao Street, Chanum Street, Governor Pack Road, Harrison Road, Otek Street, and Tabora Park (along Magsaysay Avenue), including any road, street, right-of-way, plaza, park and other public place as terminal parking space or loading and unloading areas for passengers and goods;              c)   The Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 141-09 of Hon. Vice Mayor  Daniel  T. Fari?as ?Confirming and recognizing the designated parking and loading areas with the authorized number of units allowed, presently occupied by the different legitimate public utility jeepney associations in the City of Baguio?, was returned to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation on 26 March 2010. (Item 34, 22 March 2010 Agenda)\r\n                     (NOTE:  The above proposed ordinance was  posted in the bulletin boards of the City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library and the Health Services Office starting 23 February 2010.)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(621, NULL, '02:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'City Engineer Leo C. Bernardez Jr.', 'Letter dated 17 June 2010 of City Engineer Leo C. Bernardez Jr., submitting the status report of infrastructure projects (PPC Division) as of 14 June 2010.', '-none-', '-none-', 'furnished to the Hon. Members', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(622, NULL, '02:50:00', '-none-', 'Petition', 'officers and members of the PNR-HILLSIDE Operators and Drivers Association', 'Petition of the officers and members of the PNR-HILLSIDE Operators and Drivers Association requesting the Honorable Vice Mayor to include the matter in the agenda for discussion and pass a resolution for the BAGUIO-PLAZA-TRANCOVILLE and BAGUIO-PLAZA-AUROR', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '2nd', '2010-07-07', '0591-10', 'With the coordination of the Traffic Management Branch of the Baguio City Police Office, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to allow the Aurora Hill and Trancoville public utility vehicles traverse Harrison Road under three (3) options: \r\n\r\na.  First option, the Aurora Hill and Trancoville jeepneys will traverse Harrison Road passing thru Melvin Jones and take a right turn at the Abad Santos Drive in front of the Women and Children Protection Center, BCPO, then right turn to Lake Drive and finally right turn to Bayanihan and back to Magsaysay;\r\nb.  Second option, the said jeepneys will traverse Harrison Road, passing thru the Melvin Jones take a left turn on the road, in between Veterans Memorial Park and SSS Office, passing thru Petron, Harrison and up to Cocobank then take left turn down and turn right to Harrison Road;\r\nc. Third option, the said jeepneys traverse Harrison Road up to corner of Abad Santos Drive (before University of the Cordilleras) then take right turn, then straight to Lake Drive and turn right to Abad Santos Drive passing thru the Women and Children Protection Center, BCPO and take left turn to Harrison Road.\r\n\r\nThose vehicles traversing   Upper Bonifacio St, (both Aurora Hill and Trancoville PUJ?s) will turn left to North Drive, (Infront of DILG)   and back to Bonifacio St., towards origin. \r\nThe said public utility vehicles will also observe the Odd-Even Scheme being implemented. (CR NR. 0591-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-02-08', 'Approved (Experimental basis); Res 157, s 2010 (02 Aug 2010, 56b)', '2nd', '2010-07-07', 'Acted upon; [Forwarded to the same committee, 1st Ind, 23 Jun 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(623, NULL, '10:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Emilio B. Supsupin, City Librarian', 'Letter dated 21 June 2010 of Mr. Emilio B. Supsupin, City Librarian, requesting the transfer of the amount of P3,500.00 from Account Code No. 969 (Other  Maintenance & Operating Expenses) to Account Code No. 893) (Insurance Expenses) to cover the GSIS Ins', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster A: Budget, Appropriations and Expenditures)', '1st', NULL, '0520-10', 'The Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster A, recommends approval of the foregoing request in accordance with the Local Government Code. (CR NR. 0520-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (26 Jul 2010, 5)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(624, NULL, '02:15:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'Fairview Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 16-s-10, series of 2010, of Fairview Barangay, entitled ?A Sangguniang Barangay Resolution requesting the Sangguniang Panlungsod for their approval to transfer the alley from Christian Baptist Church to Falingchan named as ?Red Ros', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research', '2nd', NULL, '0822-10', 'The Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research recommends to have the matters considered WITHDRAWN with the understanding between the barangay and the affected resident that the matter on the naming of the alley will be returned to the barangay for reconsideration or further action. (CR NR. 0822-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'WITHDRAWN (27 Sep 2010, 85b)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(625, NULL, '02:15:00', '-none-', 'Undated handwritten petition', 'Mr. Marvin Acosta, et al., all concerned vendors at T. Alonzo/Magsaysay Barangays', 'Undated handwritten petition of Mr. Marvin Acosta, et al., all concerned vendors at T. Alonzo/Magsaysay Barangays, asking assistance for the immediate dismantling of alleged illegal stalls located at Rabbit Sinkhole (Tabora Park).', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the letter dated 20 July 2009 of PS/Supt. Nestor Mendoza Bergonia, Officer-in-Charge, Baguio City Police Office (BCPO), submitting their investigation report on the alleged bingo games at Sto. Ni?o Barangay (Slaughter Compound), Baguio City and stalls at the Rabbit Sinkhole, Lower Magsaysay, Baguio City and the letter dated 16 July 2009 of  PS/Supt. Nestor Mendoza Bergonia, PESE, Officer-In-Charge, Baguio City Police Office to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, submitting their investigation report and other pertinent documents regarding the bingo operation at Slaughterhouse Compound, Sto. Ni?o Barangay and Tabora Park, Magsaysay Avenue, Baguio City, which were previously forwarded to the Committee on Human Rights, Justice, Public Protection, Peace and Order and Safety, on 22 July 2010 and 25 November 2009 respectively, for information and furnished to the Hon. Members of the Sangguniang Panlungsod.)', 'Committee on Human Rights, Justice, Public Protection and Safety, Peace and Order', '2nd', NULL, '`', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(626, NULL, '03:55:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr.', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0086-10 of Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr. ?Authorizing the City Mayor to sign for and in behalf of the City Government of Baguio the Deed of Donation and acceptance between and among the City Government of Baguio and the National H', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '1st', NULL, '0339-11', 'Attached is a letter of Mr. Eduardo G. Lea?o, Regional Manager of the National Housing Authority, Region I and CAR Office addressed to the Chairman of the Committee on Laws, clarifying that the transfer of open spaces (creek, alley, and road lot) is not automatic, citing Presidential Decree No. 1216 Section 2 which provides among others, that ? ?upon their completion certified to by the authority, the roads, alleys, sidewalks and playgrounds shall be donated by the owner or developer to the city or municipality and it shall be mandatory for the local government to accept?.\r\n             Wherefore, the Committee on Laws reiterates approval of the above stated proposed resolution.\r\n    (CR NR. 0339-11)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2011-06-06', 'Unfinished (30 May 2011, 47b)', '8th', NULL, 'For Next Agenda', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(627, NULL, '10:20:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Codification Committee on Public Utilities, Traffic and Transportation', 'Letter dated 12 May 2010 of the Codification Committee on Public Utilities, Traffic and Transportation, submitting a copy of the codified Traffic Ordinances of the City of Baguio.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 033-05 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as ?Adopting a Traffic and Transportation Code for the City of Baguio?, was forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation, on 12 April 2005.)', 'furnished to the Hon. Members', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(628, NULL, '10:20:00', '-none-', 'Undated letter', 'Baguio Gold Creek Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (BAGCJODA)', 'Undated letter of the Baguio Gold Creek Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (BAGCJODA), reiterating their request to defer the implementation of Ordinance No. 08, series of 2010 and a status quo be maintained pending the approval of the  Proposed Or', '-none-', '(NOTE:   The above matter is related to the following which were forwarded to the Committee on  Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation:\r\n        a.   Letter dated 16 June 2010 of the Baguio Sabkil Labilab Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (BASLAJODA), Inc., appealing reconsideration that the implementation of City Ordinance No. 08, series of 2010 be held in abeyance and maintain status quo pending the approval of the Proposed Ordinance No. 141, s. 2009 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as.\r\n         b.     Undated letter of the Baguio Itogon-Sangilo Drivers and Operators Association (BISDOA), reiterating their request to defer the implementation of Ordinance No. 08, series of 2010 and a status quo be maintained pending the approval of the  Proposed Ordinance No. 141, s. 2009 of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as.  \r\n                (NOTE:   a]  Ord. No. 08, s. 2010 amended ordinance Numbered 33, series of 2009;\r\n                       b]  Ord. No. 33, s. 2009 declared it unlawful for Public Utility Buses (PUBs) and Jitneys (PUJs), vans for hire including freight trucks and other vehicles of similar nature, such as trucks masquerading as jeeps, to park or to use any portion of Abanao Street, Chanum Street, Governor Pack Road, Harrison Road, Otek Street, and Tabora Park (along Magsaysay Avenue), including any road, street, right-of-way, plaza, park and other public place as terminal parking space or loading and unloading areas for passengers and goods;            \r\n                     c]   The Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 141-09 of Hon. Vice Mayor  Daniel  T. Fari?as entitled, ?Confirming and recognizing the designated parking and loading areas with the authorized number of units allowed, presently occupied by the different legitimate public utility jeepney associations in the City of Baguio?, was returned to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation on 26 March 2010. (Item 34, 22 March 2010 Agenda)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', NULL, '0630-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends  that the above stated matter be transmitted to the City Mayor?s Office considering that the City Mayor executes, enforces and implements all applicable laws and ordinances relative to the governance of the city.\r\n                            The Committee also recommends that Resolution Numbered 088, series of 2008 entitled ?Resolving that, in the meantime that the legality of the Baguio City-Mangga via Tuding and Baguio-Gold Creek franchises is being discussed and considered, the holders of said franchises should not be allowed to park anywhere in the City of Baguio? and Resolution Numbered 108, series of 2008 entitled ?Resolving that those franchises already issued or granted particularly to the Baguio-Gold Creek Operators be revoked or cancelled by the Honorable Secretary Leandro R. Mendoza of the Department of Transportation and Communications? be forwarded to the City Mayor?s Office for their guidance. (CR NR. 0630-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-09-08', 'transmitted to the Office of the City Mayor, Baguio City, considering that the Honorable City Mayor executes, enforces and implements all applicable laws and ordinances relative to the governance of the city.\r\nFurther, a copy of Resolution Numbered 088, series of 2008, entitled \"Resolving that,in the meantime that the legality of the Baguio City-Mangga via Tuding and Baguio-Gold Creek franchises is being discussed and considered, the holders of said franchises should not be allowed to park anywhere in the City of Baguio\" and Resolution Numbered 108, series of 2008, entitled \"Resolving that those franchises already issued or granted particularly to the Baguio-Gold Creek Operators be revoked or cancelled by the Honorable Secretary Leandro R. Mendoza of the Department of Transportation and Communications\" be forwarded to the City Mayor\'s Office for guidance (09 Aug 2010, 69)', '4th', '2010-11-08', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
