(670, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Indorsement', 'Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. BautistaJr.', '1st Indorsement dated 04 June 2009 of then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., returning the following unsigned resolutions for being moot and academic:\r\n\r\na. Resolution Numbered 381, series of 2008, entitled ?Declaring every Friday of the week a Carless', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above resolution was forwarded to the Office of the City Mayor on 10 October 2008 and was returned unsigned to the Office of the City Secretary on 09 June 2009.)  (Item 18, 22 February 2010 Agenda)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '2nd', NULL, '00266-10', 'On September 29, 2008, the City Council in session passed and approved Resolution No. 381, series of 2008.  The same was forwarded to the Office of the Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista, Jr., for his approval.  However, on June 6, 2009, the same resolution was returned to the Office of the City Secretary, City Council unsigned for being moot and academic.  On August 19, 2009, it was indorsed to the committee for study and recommendation.\r\nSection 4, Rule IV of Resolution No. 254, series of 2004 (A resolution providing for a codified and revised Internal Rules of Procedure for the Sangguniang Panlungsod of Baguio City provides:\r\n             ?1.  Every ordinance and resolution enacted or adopted by the Sanggunian shall be presented to the Local Chief Executive.  If the Local Chief Executive approves the same, he shall affix his signature on each and every page thereof; otherwise, he shall veto it and return the same with his objections to the Sanggunian, which may proceed to reconsider the same.  The Sanggunian concerned may override the veto of the Local Chief Executive by two thirds (2/3) vote of all its members thereby making the ordinance or resolution effective for all legal intents and purposes.\r\n          2.   The veto shall be communicated by the Local Chief Executive to the Sanggunian within ten (10) days; otherwise the ordinance shall be deemed approved as if he had signed it.?\r\n          Since the provisions of Resolution No. 254, series of 2004 are clear and unambiguous, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that Resolution Numbered 381, series of 2008, be NOTED for being moot and academic.  (CR NR. 00266-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-05-04', 'NOTED - moot and academic (To Research, 07 Arpil 2010)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', 'PU 2009', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
