(675, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'South Sanitary Camp Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution Nr. 09-06-023 of South Sanitary Camp Barangay ?Approving the change of project title from ?Completion of Senior Citizen?s Hall & Multi-purpose Hall at South Sanitary Camp Barangay? to ?Improvement/Expansion of Barangay Hall at South Sa', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Works', '-none-', NULL, '929-09', 'The Committee on Public Works recommends that the above be reverted to the General Fund and the same be reappropriated.\r\n              The committee further recommends APPROVAL of the above matter and be converted into an ordinance [PO 095-09] and be approved dispensing with the readings. (CR NR. 929-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2009-09-11', 'Approved', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(676, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Gerardo Camte, President, Gabriela Silang Operators and Drivers Association (GASODA)', 'Letter dated 18 September 2009 of Mr. Gerardo Camte, President, Gabriela Silang Operators and Drivers Association (GASODA) requesting that the BCPO and its auxiliary arms be instructed to impose ?status quo? on the use of that parking-loading space for GA', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '-none-', NULL, '00278-10', 'In consonance with the two (2) proposed ordinances, PO 077-09 of Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping, Jr. and Hon. Richard A. Cari?o, entitled ?Proposed amendatory ordinance amending Ordinance No. 33, series of 2009? and PO 141-09 of Hon. Vice Mayor  Daniel  T. Fari?as, entitled ?Confirming and recognizing the designated parking and loading areas with the authorized number of units allowed, presently occupied by the different legitimate public utility jeepney associations in the City of Baguio?, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the present parking-loading  areas occupied by the three associations (and/or all the public utility jeepneys) with the minimum number of units be  MAINTAINED ON ?STATUS QUO? while awaiting their approval and promulgation. (CR NR. 00278-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 18c)', '3rd', '2010-06-07', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(677, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee Report on Garbage', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently Abled Persons', '-none-', NULL, '941-09', 'The Local Finance Committee (LFC) suggested to ease the present problem of garbage with the following to wit: \r\n1.	Certify the amount of P19M to defray expenses pf hauling to Capas, Tarlac, provided it is exclusively used for garbage hauling;\r\n2.	Authorize the payment of P8.9M from the P19M to private haulers who rendered service to the city in a similar event on August 16 to 31;\r\n3.	To authorize P2.1 M also from the P19 M for the clearing of piled up garbage representing approximately 100 truck loads;  \r\n(NOTE;  Approved during the 14 September 2009 Regular Session - Ordinance Numbered 79, series of 2009 appropriated the amount of P2,100,000.00 out of the P19,000,00.00 certified available by the Local Finance Committee in its certification dated 10 September 2009 from the surplus of the General Fund representing unused payable accounts for the hauling expenses including tipping fee of the city?s garbage to Capas, Tarlac for the clearing and hauling of piled mixed garbage at the Irisan dumpsite.)\r\n4.	The use of savings from current appropriations of the different departments to be pooled to generate the amount of P30.6 M, to cover hauling and tipping fees up to the end of this year to be implemented solely by the city;\r\n5.	Hiring of additional personnel on a casual status for 15 Drivers and 15 Helpers on a job order status.\r\nWherefore, the Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently Abled Persons reluctantly endorses the suggested solutions of the LFC subject to the following conditions:\r\n1.	The use of savings will not in anyway undermine the authorized legal benefits of the city?s employees;\r\n2.	Savings from allocations for hauling and related solid waste management projects shall be earmarked to support the requirements of the cluster MRF?s on a first come first serve basis;\r\n3.	In the event that the plan to establish an ESL is abandoned, the amount is to be realigned for the procurement of vehicles and other appropriate equipment;\r\nIt is likewise recommended that CEPMO speed up its coordination together with the Jaime V. Ongpin Foundation on whether to junk the composting plant at the dumpsite.  In the event that the recommendation is to scrap the plant, the money appropriated for its retrofitting or repair be realigned to purchase vehicles to be assigned to the MRF?s of the barangays on a first come first serve basis.  It is also recommended that 10 bioreactors be purchased on a direct purchase for obvious reasons which shall be assigned to barangay clusters on a first come first serve basis that are ready to operate.\r\nIt is likewise recommended that the requisition of seven dump trucks purchased at Subic be vigorously followed up without let up to make it operational as soon as possible.\r\nIt is moreover recommended that the completion of the retaining wall at the dumpsite be fast tracked where supervision and monitoring on a weekly basis until its completion so that the same may be used again to deposit residual waste.\r\nFinally on the term solution, a definite decision of the executive branch of the city must be communicated to this August Body, whther or not to continue with the ESL at Sto. Tomas.  If the former is true, the Executive Department is tasked to immediately start off the development of the same as the fact is, that nothing has started yet.', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Schedule for Executive-Legislative Meeting 05 Oct 2009 (28 Sep 2009, 77)', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(678, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Sworn application', 'Atty. Nicholas A. Aquino, SVP-Legal, Government Compliance Div., Fil-Estate Properties, Inc.', 'Sworn application dated 21 May 2008 submitted by Atty. Nicholas A. Aquino, SVP-Legal, Government Compliance Div., Fil-Estate Properties, Inc., for preliminary approval and locational clearance/development permit/final approval of subdivision of Northpoint', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', NULL, '999-09', 'Having satisfied the requirements provided for by PD 957, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends APPROVAL of the above application.\r\n        Attached hereto are the following for further information and guidance:\r\n1.	Memorandum Report from the Office of the City Planning and Development Coordinator;\r\n2.	Memorandum of Agreement between Fil-Estate Properties, Inc. to avail of the Socialized Housing at the NHA?s Tuba Housing Project;\r\n3.	Certificate of Registration issued by the HLURB.\r\n        Hon. Betty Lourdes F. Tabanda, Member of the Committee, signified ?For clarification on certain issues among which are: 1. where is socialized housing-Tuba or Laguna; 2.  status of old subdivision; 3, others.? (CR NR. 999-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-01-03', 'Approved', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(679, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Cordelia C. Lacsamana, OIC-Department Head, City Parks Management Office (CPMO)', 'Letter dated 22 October 2009 of Ms. Cordelia C. Lacsamana, OIC-Department Head, City Parks Management Office (CPMO), submitting updates relative to garbage collection in the city.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons', '-none-', NULL, '0047-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that the above be merely NOTED for being moot and academic. (CR NR. 0047-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(680, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. John Colalong, President, Baguio Bengao Sto. Ni?o Subdivision Jitney Operators and Drivers Association (BBSJODA)', 'Letter dated 14 December 2009 of Mr. John Colalong, President, Baguio Bengao Sto. Ni?o Subdivision Jitney Operators and Drivers Association (BBSJODA) to Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong, requesting additional one (1) unit parking slot along Lower Chugum Strt', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '-none-', NULL, '00278-10', 'In consonance with the two (2) proposed ordinances, PO 077-09 of Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping, Jr. and Hon. Richard A. Cari?o, entitled ?Proposed amendatory ordinance amending Ordinance No. 33, series of 2009? and PO 141-09 of Hon. Vice Mayor  Daniel  T. Fari?as, entitled ?Confirming and recognizing the designated parking and loading areas with the authorized number of units allowed, presently occupied by the different legitimate public utility jeepney associations in the City of Baguio?, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the present parking-loading  areas occupied by the three associations (and/or all the public utility jeepneys) with the minimum number of units be  MAINTAINED ON ?STATUS QUO? while awaiting their approval and promulgation. (CR NR. 00278-10)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation for study and recommendation; Unfinished (28 Jun 2010, 18b)', '3rd', '2010-06-07', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(681, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', '-none-', 'Hon. Senior Citizen Councilor Romulo S. Esca?o', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. SCOFAD 02-09 of Hon. Senior Citizen Councilor Romulo S. Esca?o, entitled ?Extending mortuary assistance in the amount of Two Thousand Pesos (P2,000.00) to the heirs of the registered senior citizens in the City of Baguio?. (Item 26,', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor', '-none-', NULL, '0096-10', 'The above-cited proposal have been forwarded to the Local Finance Committee for the issuance of a Certification of Availability of Funds (CAF). To the present, no response has been received by the committee.\r\n         The Committee on Social Services, Women, and Urban Poor recommends that pending the issuance of the CAF by the Local Finance Committee, the above matter be forwarded to the concerned department for possible inclusion in their regular activities, to be funded under their respective department budget. (CR NR. 0096-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to OCSWDO through Ms. Betty F. Fangasan, Baguio City, for possible inclusion in their regular activities, to be funded under their respective department\'s budget, pending the issuance of the CAF by the Local Finance Committee (22 Feb 2010, 131)', '4th', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(682, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'East Bayan Park Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 16, series of 2009, of East Bayan Park Barangay, Aurora Hill, Baguio City, entitled ?Requesting the Honorable Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. thru the Local Finance Committee for the realignment of the unimplemented  project fund ou', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Works', '-none-', NULL, '0147-10', 'The Committee on Public Works recommends that the above be reverted to the General Fund and the same be reappropriated.\r\n        The committee further recommends APPROVAL of the above matter and be converted into an ordinance [PO Nr. 0018-10] and be approved dispensing with the readings. (CR NR. 0147-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-08-03', 'Approved (8 Mar 2010, 32)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(683, NULL, '10:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Dir. Joel G. Salvador, Regional Director, Environmental Management Bureau (EMB), DENR-CAR', 'Letter dated 20 August 2004 of Dir. Joel G. Salvador, Regional Director, Environmental Management Bureau (EMB), DENR-CAR, informing that the DENR-CAR, in its commitment for environmental protection and preservation, acknowledges the chairmanship of the Ta', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The proposed resolution above-mentioned is under Proposed Resolution Nr. 180-04 entitled ?A resolution to create a Taskforce to address the July 01, 2004 petition of residents along Magsaysay Avenue, Baguio City, on the matters of ill effects of polluted air, land and water from the polluted creek originating from Burnham Lake traversing underneath Magsaysay Avenue, Slaughter Compound and openly passing through Barangay private Road, Magsaysay Avenue, Sanitary Camp, Baguio City and down to La Trinidad Valley.?)', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons', '1st', NULL, '0159-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons acknowledges the Chairmanship of the DENR-CAR for the Task Force created under Resolution Nr. 219, series of 2004 and that a monthly report concerning the above be given to the Members of the City Council for their information and guidance. (CR NR. 0159-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-01-03', 'Returned to Mr. Paquito T. Moreno, Jr., Regional Director, Environement Mangement Bureau (EMB), DENR-CAR, with the information that the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio acknowledges the chairmanship of the DENR-CAR for the Task Force created under Resolution Nr. 219, series of 2004 and that a monthly report concerning the above be given to the Honorable Members of the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio, for their information and guidance (1 Mar 2010, 77)', '3rd', '2010-09-03', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(684, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Board Resolution', 'Scout Barrio Bayanihan Multipurpose Cooperative, of Scout Barrio, Baguio City', 'Board Resolution dated February 2010 of Scout Barrio Bayanihan Multipurpose Cooperative, of Scout Barrio, Baguio City, entitled ?A resolution requesting the City Government of Baguio to extend financial loan to the Scout Barrio Bayanihan Multipurpose Coop', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Employment, Livelihood and Cooperatives', '-none-', NULL, '0160-10', 'The Committee on Employment, Livelihood and Cooperatives, after finding that the water refilling station is a felt need of Scout Barrio, Baguio City, hereby recommends that the said resolution be referred to the Office of Hon. Mauricio G. Domogan and accompanied by the favorable indorsement of the same by the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio City. (CR NR. 0160-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-01-03', 'referred to the Office of Hon. Mauricio G. Domogan and accompanied by the favorable indorsement of the same by the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio City (1 Mar 2010, 78)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(685, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Matter', 'diarrhea in Navy Base Pacdal Baguio City', 'Matter relative to the cause/causes of diarrhea in Navy Base Pacdal Baguio City for the information of the city Council in order to find solutions to prevent the repetition of the situation described above for the protection for the health of the constitu', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 127-09 of Hon. Erdolfo V. Balajadia ?Inviting in aid of legislation the Health Services Officer, the Baguio Water District Officer and the City Environment Management Officer to shed light on the cause/causes of diarrhea in Navy Base Pacdal Baguio City for the information of the City Council in order to find solutions to prevent the repetition of the situation described above for the protection for the health of the  health of the constituents of the City of Baguio?  was approved  during the 22 June 2009 Regular Session and the personalities cited in the proposal were invited to shed light on the above matter during the 29 June 2009 Regular Session.)', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that the above was discussed and determined during the 29 June 2009 Agenda. Furthermore, that the said situation be NOTED co', '-none-', NULL, '1021-09', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that the above was discussed and determined during the 29 June 2009 Agenda. Furthermore, that the said situation be NOTED considering that the agencies concerned have already undertaken measures to prevent the repetition of the incident above stated. (CR NR. 1021-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(686, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Punong Barangay Jesusa Lucio-Vizcaya of Loakan Proper Barangay', 'Letter dated 07 April 2009 of Punong Barangay Jesusa Lucio-Vizcaya of Loakan Proper Barangay to Ms. Teresita de Guzman, General Manager, Baguio Water District (BWD), forwarding Resolution No. 20, series of 2009, entitled ?A resolution endorsing Resolution', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '1031-09', 'Guided by the policy of putting general welfare and delivery of basic social services to its constituents as the councils? thrust, the Sangguniang Panlungsod passed City Ordinance No. 67, series of 2009, granting ?amnesty? to building and structure owners without building permits to have electric or water connections from the BENECO and BWD.\r\n      The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the request of the residents of Km. 6 Sto. Tomas, Dontogan and Purok Magsaysay, Loakan Proper be NOTED with the passage of Ordinance No. 67, s. 2009. Further, request BWD to facilitate or fast track the installation of pipelines thereat and connect water supply to households after complying with the requirements provided under Ordinance No. 67, s. 2009. (CR NR. 1031-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(687, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Richard L. Bagawi, President, Quezon Hill Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (QUIHODA)', 'Letter dated 21 October 2009 of Mr. Richard L. Bagawi, President, [Quezon] Quirino Hill Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (QUIHODA) to Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong, seeking for a status quo on the implementation of Administrative Order No. 108, s', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Adm. Order 108, s. 2006, entitled ?Continuance of the experimental re-routing scheme of Quirino Hill Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (QUIHODA) with amendments and conditions.?)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '-none-', NULL, '1092-09', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the matter be DISCUSSED EN BANC. Recommending further that the affected association, through its President and representative(s) of the Traffic management Group be invited to clarify and answer queries from the members of the Honorable City Council in its regular session on November 9, 2009. (CR NR. 1092-09)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved as amended', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(688, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 117-09 of Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen, entitled \"Naming the streets, alleys, passageways and maintain road/s of Pinget Barangay\".', '-none-', '(NOTE: [a]  FIRST READING -09 November 2009\r\n[b]     SECOND READING AND FOR PUBLICATION -07 December 2009\r\n              - Posted in the bulletin boards of City Hall, City Public Market, Post Office, City Library and the Health Services Office starting 09 December 2009;         \r\n  [c]     The above proposed ordinance was adopted from Barangay Ordinance No. 01, series of 2009, of Pinget Barangay, entitled ?An ordinance naming of streets, alleys, passageways and mainroad of Pinget Barangay.?\r\n(Item 65, 07 June 2010 Agenda)', 'Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research', '3rd', '2009-11-11', '00429-10', 'The Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research recommends APPROVAL of the above proposed ordinance on THIRD AND FINAL READING.  (CR NR. 00429-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved (21 Jun 2010, 73)', '7th', '2010-09-06', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(689, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 122-09 of Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen ?Naming the alleys and bridges/roads of Imelda Village Barangay, Baguio City.', '-none-', '(NOTE: The above proposed ordinance was adopted from the Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009, of Imelda Village Barangay, entitled \"Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009 for the naming of existing Purok alleys and bridges/roads with the jurisdiction of the barangay.\") (Item 65, 09 November 2009 Agenda)', 'Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research', '3rd', '2009-01-12', '00382-10', 'The Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research recommends the APPROVAL of the above proposed ordinance on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION. (CR NR. 00382-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-07-06', 'APPROVAL of the above proposed ordinance on SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION (7 Jun 2010, 64)', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending (related to Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009, of Imelda Village Barangay, entitled ?Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009 for the naming of existing Purok alleys and bridges/roads within the jurisdiction of the barangay.?)', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
