(1337, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Elmer O. Datuin', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 170-06 of Hon. Elmer O. Datuin ?Granting yearly cash incentives to all employees of the Public Attorneys Office, Parole and Probation Office, Municipal Trial Courts and the Regional Trial Courts of Baguio City.?', '170-06', '(NOTE:  [a]  FIRST READING ? 04 December 2006]', 'Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel', '1st', '2006-07-12', '0317-11', 'The Committee on  Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel recommends that PO 170-06 of Hon. Datuin be NOTED considering that they are covered by the rationalization of allowance, benefits and incentives. Likewise the 4th indorsement dated dated 07 February 2011 from the Local Finance Committee answering the same request by Atty. Ruth Bawayan, et al. expressing unfavorable recommendation due to the lack of funds and the city is exceeding its personal services ceiling which would bar further granting honoraria to employees of national offices.\r\n              Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez, Member of the Committee, signified ?Pls. refer to the Local Finance Committee.?\r\n              Hon. Edison R. Bilog, Member of the Committee, signified ?for discussion en banc.? The matter on the request of Atty. Bawayan, et al. is different from the request of the PAO, on the following grounds:\r\n     1) There is a law that authorizes the said allowance to be given to PAO lawyers;\r\n     2) My proposed ordinance seeks to incorporate the allowance of PAO lawyers with the 2012 Budget, thus there would be funding for this purpose and the problem on the personal services ceiling would be addressed. (CR NR. 0317-11)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Deferred - returned to committee for further study (23 May 2011, 39)', '3rd', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
