(1842, '2005-02-02', '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Request', 'Mr. Roberto R. Gonzales, President,Taripnong Ti Mangmanged, noted by Mr. Rodolfo De Leon Paragas, Consultant-Adviser and Spokesperson, Taripnong Ti Mangmanged, Upper Session Road, Inc.', 'Request dated 01 February 2005 of Mr. Roberto R. Gonzales, President,Taripnong Ti Mangmanged, noted by Mr. Rodolfo De Leon Paragas, Consultant-Adviser and Spokesperson, Taripnong Ti Mangmanged, Upper Session Road, Inc., for the segregation of the lots the', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', '2005-04-02', '01020-10', 'The above proposed resolution and requests are for the segregation of a portion of Proclamation No. 820, series of 1935, which revoked Proclamation No. 65, series of 1925 and reserving the same parcel of land described therein for school and other public purposes under the administration of the City of Baguio. In the process of any issuance of proclamation/segregation, the requirements, among others, are: a request from the reservee; comments and recommendation of offices such as the Department of  Education or District/City Superintendent of the school, including the justification, legal basis of such request and potential problems, if any, pursuant to MC No. 28, series of 1993 of the Land Management Bureau, DENR.\r\n         Considering the hereto attached letter dated 30 November 2010 of ELLEN B. DONATO, Ed. D., CESO IV, School Superintendent, Division of Baguio City, Department of Education-CAR, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing respectfully regrets that the above proposed resolution and requests cannot be favorably acted upon.\r\n      The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing strongly recommends:\r\n     1. To ENDORSE the relocation of the above affected families to that site at Teacher?s Camp, covered by Proclamation 613 under the administration of the National Housing Authority, considering that Proclamation 613 is a project of the National Housing Authority and the Department of Education, Culture and Historical Research for Dep-Ed employees and the petitioners who are also mostly current and former Dep-Ed employees/dependents;\r\n     2. To REQUEST the National Housing Authority, Region I/CAR Administrator  of the relocation site to prioritize the above families, subject to guidelines;\r\n     3. To REQUEST the Baguio City Schools Division, Department of Education-CAR to assist the affected families to facilitate their relocation and to allow the occupants to temporarily stay in the area until such time they have been relocated, provided that there shall be no expansion, construction of permanent structures or future request for segregation on the part of the occupants. (CR NR. 01020-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'the above proposed resolution and requests cannot be favorably acted upon.\r\n      The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing strongly recommends:\r\n     1. To ENDORSE the relocation of the above affected families to that site at Teacher?s Camp, covered by Proclamation 613 under the administration of the National Housing Authority, considering that Proclamation 613 is a project of the National Housing Authority and the Department of Education, Culture and Historical Research for Dep-Ed employees and the petitioners who are also mostly current and former Dep-Ed employees/dependents;\r\n     2. To REQUEST the National Housing Authority, Region I/CAR Administrator  of the relocation site to prioritize the above families, subject to guidelines;\r\n     3. To REQUEST the Baguio City Schools Division, Department of Education-CAR to assist the affected families to facilitate their relocation and to allow the occupants to temporarily stay in the area until such time they have been relocated, provided that there shall be no expansion, construction of permanent structures or future request for segregation on the part of the occupants (31 Jan 2011, 39d)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
