(2150, '2010-11-03', '09:50:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Merlyn Palaganas, President, Baguio Mantas Swim Club', 'Letter dated 03 March 2010 of Ms. Merlyn Palaganas, President, Baguio Mantas Swim Club, asking consideration for the amendment of City Ordinance No. 34, series of 2004, since most of the swimmers are children who attend classes from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Ord. No. 34, series of 2004, Established the general guidelines for the management operation and maintenance of the swimming pool complex at the Baguio Athletic Bowl.)', 'Committee on Laws', '4th', '2010-12-03', '00362-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends that the above stated matter be NOTED, considering that the Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as has filed Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0026-10 entitled ?Amending Section 3.1 of Ordinance Numbered 34, series of 2004 and providing funds from the Annual City Budget for the maintenance of the Swimming Pool complex at the Baguio Athletic Bowl?. (CR NR. 00362-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (21 Jun 2010, 41)', '6th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2151, '2010-11-03', '10:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Wene Cawayan, et al., all members of the Baguio-Bayabas Joint Operators-Drivers Association (BBJODA)', 'Letter dated 10 March 2010 of Mr. Wene Cawayan, et al., all members of the Baguio-Bayabas Joint Operators-Drivers Association (BBJODA), requesting exemption from the implementation of the odd-even traffic scheme.', '-none-', '(NOTE: A motion requesting the Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr. to exempt the jeepneys plying the Bayabas, alno and Balili routes from the application of the number coding scheme and to apply to them th \"1-2-1-2\" scheme was adopted on 01 March 2010 Regular Session)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '2nd', '2010-12-03', '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2152, '2010-11-03', '04:50:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Hon. Nestor B. Fongwan, Provincial Governor, Province of Benguet', 'Letter dated 08 March 2010 of Hon. Nestor B. Fongwan, Governor, Province of Benguet, on the following:\r\na. expressing sincere thanks to the City Council regarding the issues they raised in the implementation of the traffic scheme that affected the La Trin', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '6th', '2010-08-07', '0453-10', 'With the foregoing reasons stated in its 2nd Indorsement dated 17 May 2010, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to APPROVE that the BUHAGAN ROAD (formerly Bokawkan Road) be OPENED for the public utility jitneys associations with more than twenty units and observing the ?odd-even scheme?:\r\n           Further recommending to APPROVE that all public utility buses and vans-for-hire parked under a contract of lease or agreement with the Dangwa Terminal Compound or its leasing company be relocated to the Slaughter Terminal, Sto. Ni?o Barangay and only public utility jitneys be allowed to park and load/unload at the Dangwa Terminal Compound.\r\n           Recommending finally to APPROVE that all structures or shanties built at the Tabora Park area be demolished and prohibit any person from installing any structure or shanty for the purpose of trade, business or quarters.  The Tabora Park shall be converted as a staging area for all other public utility jitneys not accommodated at the Dangwa Terminal Compound. (CR NR. 0453-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation;  Deferred (28 Jun 2010, 5c9)', '6th', '2010-08-07', 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the same committee, 2nd Ind, 12 Mar 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2153, '2010-12-03', '02:55:00', '-none-', 'Photocopy of the agreement', 'Pico Puguis-Long Long-Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association', 'Photocopy of the agreement of the Pico Puguis-Long Long-Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association, to utilize the portion of land located between Rizal Park Barangay and City Hall as their loading area.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The letter dated 09 March 2010 of Mr. Aurelio D. Placido, President, Pico, Puguis, Longlong, Motorpool Jeepney Operators and Drivers Association (PPLMJODA) to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, requesting that their association be included in the agenda for discussion/deliberation by the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio in relation to the endorsement dated 16 February 2010 of the Hon. Congressman Samuel M. Dangwa endorsing Resolution 1-2010, of the Sangguniang Bayan of La Trinidad, Benguet, that said association be allowed to ply the route La Trinidad to Baguio via Bokawkan/Buhagan Road, was previously forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation.)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation for information and to be attached to the Ind. (Letter date 09 March 2010 of Mr. Placido)', '6th', '2010-08-07', '0453-10', 'With the foregoing reasons stated in its 2nd Indorsement dated 17 May 2010, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to APPROVE that the BUHAGAN ROAD (formerly Bokawkan Road) be OPENED for the public utility jitneys associations with more than twenty units and observing the ?odd-even scheme?:\r\n           Further recommending to APPROVE that all public utility buses and vans-for-hire parked under a contract of lease or agreement with the Dangwa Terminal Compound or its leasing company be relocated to the Slaughter Terminal, Sto. Ni?o Barangay and only public utility jitneys be allowed to park and load/unload at the Dangwa Terminal Compound.\r\n           Recommending finally to APPROVE that all structures or shanties built at the Tabora Park area be demolished and prohibit any person from installing any structure or shanty for the purpose of trade, business or quarters.  The Tabora Park shall be converted as a staging area for all other public utility jitneys not accommodated at the Dangwa Terminal Compound. (CR NR. 0453-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation; Deferred (28 Jun 2010, 5c3)', '6th', '2010-08-07', 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation for information and to be attached to the Ind. (Letter date 09 March 2010 of Mr. Placido), 1st Ind, 16 Mar 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2154, '2010-12-03', '02:55:00', '-none-', 'Joint opposition', 'Mr. Marcelo Lagda, President, Navy Base Transport Operators and Drivers Association (NBTODA) and Mr. Melchor Bengaw, President, Pacdal General Luna Operators and Drivers Association (PAGODA)', 'Joint opposition dated 12 March 2010 submitted by Mr. Marcelo Lagda, President, Navy Base Transport Operators and Drivers Association (NBTODA) and Mr. Melchor Bengaw, President, Pacdal General Luna Operators and Drivers Association (PAGODA), to the Propos', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0042-10 of Hon. Richard A. Cari?o ?Recommending to the Land Transportation Franchising and Regulatory Board (LTFRB) the legalization of irregular and illegal franchises of public utility vehicles in Baguio City and Cordillera Administrative Region (CAR), subject to conditions?, was forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation on 16 February 2010.)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '1st', NULL, '00129-13', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislations recommends approval of the herein attached amended Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0030-13 of Hon. Richard A. Cari?o and    Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping Jr., consolidating all the above subject matter. Final lists of public utility vehicles which were \"irregularly issued\"/issued in violation of LTFRB MC 1996-002 (Baguio Moratorium) and LTFRB MC 98-026 (BLIST Moratorium), prepared by DOTC-CAR received by the undersigned Chairperson on February 20, 2013 is likewise attached. (CR NR. 00129-13); After series of public consultation and with coordination with the Department of Transportation and Communication ? Cordillera Administrative Region (DOTC-CAR) through the Office of Regional Director Celina B. Claver, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends approval of the amended proposed resolution.  Final lists of public utility vehicles which were ?irregularly issued?/issued in violation of LTFRB MC 1996-002 (Baguio Moratorium) and LTFRB MC 98-026 (BLIST Moratorium) prepared by DOTC-CAR is hereto attached which was received by the undersigned chairman on March 9, 2012. (CR NR. 0166-12)', '0000-00-00', '2026-06-02', NULL, '[Forwarded back to committee, 9th Ind., 09 July 2013]; Unfinished (17 Jun 2013, 29g); Unfinished (10 Jun 2013, 30g); Unfinished (27 May 2013, 31g); Unfinished (20 May 2013, 32g); Unfinished (06 May 2013, 31g); Unfinished (29 Apr 2013, 32g); Unfinished (22 Apr 2013, 33g); Unfinished (15 Apr 2013, 35g); Unfinished (08 Apr 2013, 38g); Unfinished (01 Apr 2013, 57g); Unfinished (18 Mar 2013, 58g); Unfinished (11 Mar 2013, 68g); Deferred - returned to committee for further study and to consider the statements of hon. Nicasio S. Palaganas during the 14 January 2013 Regular Session (14 Jan 2013, 3g); Invite Dir. Claver on January 14, 2013 RS (07 Jan 2013, 4g); Unfinished (17 Dec 2012, 5g); Unfinished (10 Dec 2012, 4g); Unfinished (03 Dec 2012, 4g); Unfinished (26 Nov 2012, 3g); Unfinished (19 Nov 2012, 3g); Unfinished (12 Nov 2012, 3g); Unfinished (05 Nov 2012, 4g); Unfinished (22 Oct 2012, 4g); Unfinished (08 Oct 2012, 8g); Unfinished (08 Oct 2012, 8g); Unfinished (24 Sep 2012, 10g); Unfinished (17 Sep 2012, 13g); Unfinished (10 Sep 2012, 14g); Unfinished (03 Sep 2012, 17g); Unfinished (13 Aug 2012, 14g); Unfinished (06 Aug 2012, 13g); Unfinished (30 Jul 2012, 14g); Unfinished (23 Jul 2012, 13g); Unfinished (09 Jul 2012, 17g); Unfinished (02 Jul 2012, 20g); Deferred (25 Jun 2012, 19g); Unfinished (18 Jun 2012, 20g); Unfinished (11 Jun 2012, 29g); Unfinished (04 Jun 2012, 28g); Deferred (21 May 2012, 17g); Unfinished (14 May 2012, 19g); Unfinished (07 May 2012, 23g); Unfinished (23 Apr 2012, 31g); Unfinished (16 apr 2012, 65g);', '9th', '2013-09-07', 'Pending; [Related to PR 0042-10]; [Forwarded back to committee, 9th Ind., 09 July 2013];', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
