(2317, '2010-06-04', '11:05:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Director Clarence L. Baguilat, CESO III, Regional Executive Director, DENR-CAR', 'Letter dated 26 March 2010 of Director Clarence L. Baguilat, CESO III, Regional Executive Director, DENR-CAR. acknowledging receipt of the letter dated 23 March 2010 of Ms. Maria Remedios C. Agranzamendez, Local Legislative Staff Officer V, regarding Reso', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Res. No. 029, s. 2010 requested the Department of Environment and Natural Resources-Cordillera Administrative Region (DENR-CAR) to include the survey of all identified city/barangay needs in its TS-CAR Baguio City Project for Final Lot and Adjustment of old Surveys.)', 'furnished to the Hon. Members & Research div. (attach as supp. doc. of Res. No. 029, s. 2010)', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', 'Research Division', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2318, '2010-06-04', '09:45:00', '-none-', 'Letter-petition', 'Hotel and Restaurant Association of Baguio City and concerned constituents of the City of Baguio', 'Letter-petition dated 18 March 2010 of the members of Hotel and Restaurant Association of Baguio City and concerned constituents of the City of Baguio, to declare the Filipino Society of Composers, Authors and Publishers Inc. (FILSCAP) among others on the', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the letter dated 05 September 2008 of Atty. Mos P. Cating, Chairman, Hotel & Restaurant Association of Baguio (HRAB) to Hon. Fred L. Bagbagen, seeking assistance on the letter dated 22 August 2008 of Ms. Ivy C. Labayne, Filipino Society of Composers, Authors & Publishers, Inc., (FILSCAP), regarding unauthorized public performance of copyright music, which was returned to the Committee on Laws on 08 October 2008, for further study.)', 'Committee on Laws', '2nd', '2010-07-04', '0361-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends that the above matter be NOTED, considering that City Council Resolution Numbered 079, series of 2010, entitled ?Declaring Ms. Debbie Gaite, Ms. Tina Belamide, Mr. Heber Bartolome, Mr. Mike Villegas, Mr. Mel Villena, Mr. Jovencio Aguilar, and Mr. Danny Fabella, Officers and Members of the Filipino Society of Composers, Authors and Publishers Inc. (FILSCAP)  PERSONA NON GRATA in the City of Baguio for having authored maligning, slurring and wantonly defamatory words against the people of Baguio? was adopted during the City Council Regular Session held on April 12, 2010. (CR NR. 0361-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (21 Jun 2010, 40)', '4th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
(2319, '2010-06-04', '03:05:00', '-none-', 'Undated motion', 'Mr. Miguel P. Luma-ang, President, Federation of Jeepney Associations, La Trinidad Trunkline, La Trinidad, Benguet', 'Undated motion for reconsideration of Mr. Miguel P. Luma-ang, President, Federation of Jeepney Associations, La Trinidad Trunkline, La Trinidad, Benguet, requesting among others the following:\r\n?a. to shorten the two (2) months experimental period granted', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '6th', '2010-08-07', '0453-10', 'With the foregoing reasons stated in its 2nd Indorsement dated 17 May 2010, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends to APPROVE that the BUHAGAN ROAD (formerly Bokawkan Road) be OPENED for the public utility jitneys associations with more than twenty units and observing the ?odd-even scheme?:\r\n           Further recommending to APPROVE that all public utility buses and vans-for-hire parked under a contract of lease or agreement with the Dangwa Terminal Compound or its leasing company be relocated to the Slaughter Terminal, Sto. Ni?o Barangay and only public utility jitneys be allowed to park and load/unload at the Dangwa Terminal Compound.\r\n           Recommending finally to APPROVE that all structures or shanties built at the Tabora Park area be demolished and prohibit any person from installing any structure or shanty for the purpose of trade, business or quarters.  The Tabora Park shall be converted as a staging area for all other public utility jitneys not accommodated at the Dangwa Terminal Compound. (CR NR. 0453-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation;Deferred (28 Jun 2010, 5c4)', '6th', '2010-08-07', 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the same committee, 1st Ind, 08 Apr 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:42'),
