(3117, NULL, '03:20:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'Dontogan Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 10, series of 2010, of Dontogan Barangay, entitled ?A resolution of the Sangguniang Barangay of Dontogan identifying and naming interior streets, roads and alleys within Dontogan Barangay.?', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Education, Culture and Historical  Research', '1st', NULL, 'EDUC-2017-029', 'The Committee on Education, Culture and Historical Research recommends that the matter be NOTED with the reiteration of the earlier advise to the barangay to consider the National Historical Commission of the Philippines (NHCP) Guidelines on the renaming of streets, alleys and barangays, a copy of which is herewith provided for easy reference. (EDUC-2017-029).', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2017-06-11', 'NOTED; informed proponent as per the letter dated 07 November 2017 (06 November 2017, 42); cancelled session (30 October 2017).', '-none-', NULL, 'FOR NEXT AGENDA', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3118, NULL, '03:20:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Ordinance', 'Dontogan Barangay', 'Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009, of Dontogan Barangay, entitled ?An ordinance amending Section 4 of Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2005 [Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2005 was enacted by the Sangguniang Barangay of Do', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above is in reply to the 3rd Indorsement dated 01 March 2010 of the Office of the City Secretary returning to Punong Barangay Henry F. Figueras, Dontogan Barangay, Baguio City, the Barangay Ordinance Numbered 01, series of 2009, of Dontogan Barangay, for review by the Barangay Council to consider the following observations of the Honorable Members of the Sangguniang Panlungsod ng Baguio:\r\na.	Item c, Sec. 6 ? Aren?t streets and roads beyond the commerce of man?;\r\nb.	Sec. 7 ? Identifying/naming roads and alleys must be covered by a separate ordinance;\r\nc.	Sec. 8 ? the creation of a barangay logo shall be covered by a separate ordinance;\r\nd.	for the barangay to adhere to the approved City Tax Ordinance 2000-001 with regards to the collection of fees for parking and garbage; and\r\ne.	to take note that the barangay can only collect from private residence households and apartments and not business proprietors,\r\nper amended report of the Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster C, acted upon during the 22 February 2010 Regular Session.)', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster C: Review of Barangay Budgets and Barangay Tax Ordinances; Accrediation of NGOs and other concerns)', '1st', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
