(3123, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Joint Resolution', 'Office of the Deputy Ombudsman For Luzon', 'Joint Resolution dated 11 January 2010 issued by the Office of the Deputy Ombudsman For Luzon on the twin complaint filed by Mr. Roberto Ocampo against Punong Barangay Antonino A. Cortez Jr., Barangay Kagawads Melvin A Cortes, Nelia V. Preposi, Joven S. G', '-none-', '(The above matter is related to the letter dated 18 July 2008 of Mr.  Roberto Ocampo, forwarding his affidavit-complaint under oath against Barangay Officials  Antonino A. CortezJr., Melvin A Cortes, Nelia Proposi, Noel A. Abrasaldo, Jaime P. Cabiles, Joven Garcia, Juan Teodolfo  Gascon and  Edilberto Bautista, et al.,  Bayan Park Village Barangay which was docketed as SP Adm. Case No. 04-2008 which was forwarded  to Division I [Ad Hoc Committee on Barangay Administrative Cases].)', 'To Division I (Ad Hoc Committee on Barangay Administrative Cases) for information', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3124, NULL, '01:30:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Hon. Joel A. Alangsab, ABC President/SP Member II, Office of the Liga President', 'Letter dated 23 March 2010 of Hon. Joel A. Alangsab, ABC President/SP Member II, Office of the Liga President to Punong Barangay Vicente S. Pinlac, AZKCO Barangay endorsing their Barangay Resolution No. 5, series of 2010, entitled ? A resolution approving', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '1st', NULL, '00354-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends DENIAL based on the following:\r\n1.	No fund-raising activity may be held within sixty (60) days prior to or after an election Pursuant to Art. 101, paragraph a, number 11, of the Local Government Code, to wit:\r\n           Hold fund-raising activities for barangay projects without the need of securing permits from any national or local office or agency. The proceeds from such activities shall be tax-exempt and shall accrue to the general fund of the barangay provided that in the appropriation thereof, the specific purpose for which such fund-raising activity has been held shall be first satisfied and provided further, that no fund-raising activities shall be held within a period of sixty (60) days immediately preceding and after a national or local election, recall, referendum, or plebiscite (underscoring ours).\r\n2.	The CEPMO is denying the request, pursuant to Sec. 2 of CO No. 10, series of 2008, to wit:\r\n                 It is hereby declared a policy of the Local Government of Baguio City to regulate trade fairs in the City of Baguio by allowing the conduct of trade fairs for a period of not exceeding 15 days in suitable public or private places, except in Burnham Park, the People?s Park, and other city-owned or city-managed public parks within the Central Business District, that promote agricultural, industrial, indigenous and commercial products, crafts, and other merchandise through inter-regional trading that will foster better livelihood opportunities, enhance local tourism, and help advance economic development. \r\n        Hon. Richard A. Cari?o, Member of the Committee, signified ?for discussion?. (CR NR. 00354-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Forwarded to the Committee on Laws with the information that the above matters were noted during the 17 May 2010 Regular Session and for the committee to come up with a clearer report (17 May 2010, 56a)', '3rd', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
