(3130, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Florfina Palas', 'Letter dated 06 March 2010 of Ms. Florfina Palas to Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., seeking assistance to secure a building permit and for the removal of a fence put up by a certain Engr. Espejo over her property located at Paterno St., South Drive, Baguio C', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '-none-', NULL, '0703-10', 'The Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the above be FORWARDED to the following offices for appropriate action:\r\n1. The City Buildings and Architecture Office on the matter of securing a building permit.\r\n2. The City Legal Office on the mater of the removal of fence by Engr. Espejo. (CR NR. 0703-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-06-09', 'FORWARDED to the following offices for appropriate action:\r\n1. to Engr. Oscar V. Flores, City Buildings and Architecture Office (CBAO), Baguio City, on the matter of securing a building permit; and\r\n2. to Atty. Melchor Carlos R. Rabanes, OIC, City Legal Office, Baguio City, on the mater of the removal of fence by Engr. Espejo (06 Sep 2010, 17)', '3rd', '2010-07-09', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3131, NULL, '11:25:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Dr. Ambeth R. Ocampo, DPA, Chairman, National Historical Institute', 'Letter dated 12 March 2010 of Dr. Ambeth R. Ocampo, DPA, Chairman, National Historical Institute, informing to Hon. Lyn Danao-Moreno, CESO II, Assistant Executive Secretary, General Government Administration Office, Office of the President of the Philippi', '-none-', '(NOTE:  Ordinance Nr. 81, s. 2009, entitled ?Officially renaming the Baguio Botanical and Zoological Garden as Baguio Centennial and Botanical Park.?)', 'furnished to the Hon. Members & Research Div. (attach as supp. doc. of Ord. Nr. 81, s. 2009)', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3132, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Barangay Resolution', 'Kayang Hilltop  Barangay', 'Barangay Resolution No. 007, series of 2010, of Kayang Hilltop  Barangay, entitled ?A resolution allowing Librada Macalindong bingo amusement operator to conduct/operate bingo amusement in a designated area at Barangay Kayang Hilltop, Baguio City for fund', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Laws', '-none-', NULL, '00314-10', 'The Committee on Laws recommends to return the above sated barangay resolution without council approval due to the following reasons:\r\n1.	The resolution did not specify the period of the bingo operation, considering that Sec. 391 par. 11 of the Local Government Code provides that, no fund raising activities shall be held within a period of six (60) days immediately preceding and after a national or local election, recall, referendum, or plebiscite;\r\n2.	The resolution did not mention the designated area where the said fund raising activity will be conducted; and\r\n3.	As a character city, the activity is inconsistent with approved city ordinances and resolutions. (CR NR. 00314-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Returned to Punong Barangay Julita R. Sino-Cruz, Kayang Hilltop Barangayt, Baguio City, without Council approval due to the following reasons:\r\n1.	The resolution did not specify the period of the bingo operation, considering that Sec. 391 par. 11 of the Local Government Code provides that, no fund raising activities shall be held within a period of six (60) days immediately preceding and after a national or local election, recall, referendum, or plebiscite;\r\n2.	The resolution did not mention the designated area where the said fund raising activity will be conducted; and\r\n3.	As a character city, the activity is inconsistent with approved city ordinances and resolutions. (26 Apr 2010, 50)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3133, '2010-05-04', '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Hon. Galo D. Weygan', 'Letter dated 05 April 2010 of then City Councilor Galo D. Weygan, requesting to deliver his privilege speech, entitled ?Making Baguio a Character City is Everybody?s Business?.', '-none-', '(NOTE:  [a] With marginal notation of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as ?Approved   provided members will not object?. ?Jun, Please take note.?\r\n             [b] The privilege speech of former Coun. Galo D. Weygan was foregone during the 26 April 2010  Agenda) (Item 72, 27 September 2010 Agenda)', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '0063-11', 'The Committee on Ethics, Governmental Affairs and Personnel  recommends that PO 002-10 of former Coun. Galo D. Weygan, et. Al entitled ?Institutionalizing the existence and operation of the Baguio Character Council created under Resolution 107, series of 2003?,  BE NOTED as it is already consolidated in PO 0095-10.\r\n               Further, the committee recommends that consolidated ordinance be  APPROVED  on its SECOND READING AFTER PUBLICATION. The proposed consolidation of  Ordinance Nr. PO 002-10 and PO 0095-10 of Hon. Philian Louise Weygan-Allan entitled, ?The Character City Ordinance of the City of Baguio?, as amended was approved on Second Reading after publication and posting in the 4th Indorsement dated 21 October 2010 showing the following new items revision as a result of the consolidation:\r\na.	Fourth paragraph as a new item ?City Resolution Numbered 343, series of 2009 declared every third week of the September as Character Week in the City of Baguio?;\r\nb.	SECTION 8 :Fiscal Requirement item 1.a. Salary ?Administrative  Aide VI (Clerk III) SG 6/1 account title worth P156,000.00 was changed to an account title ?Character Night Activity? with the same amount. (CR NR. 0063-11)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2011-09-05', 'returned to committee for further study (09 May 2011, 16b.2); returned to committee for consolidation of the proposals (with PO 002-10 and PO 0095-10) (22 Nov 2010, 50b)', '16th', '2011-10-05', 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3134, '2010-05-04', '10:10:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Galo D. Weygan, Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong, Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez, Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping Jr., Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., Hon. Joel A. Alangsab and Hon. Gloria Ysabel V. De Vera', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0033-10 of then City Councilor Galo D. Weygan, Hon. Rocky Thomas A. Balisong, Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez, Hon. Nicasio M. Aliping Jr., Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., Hon. Joel A. Alangsab and Hon. Gloria Ysabel V. De Vera ?Authori', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Employment, Livelihood and Cooperatives', '1st', '2010-06-04', '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Referral to Committee (5 Apr 2010, 56)', '-none-', NULL, 'Pending', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3135, '2010-05-04', '11:05:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Punong Barangay Catherine A. Qui?ones, MRR Queen of Peace Barangay', 'Letter dated 05 April 2010 of Punong Barangay Catherine A. Qui?ones, MRR Queen of Peace Barangay, resubmitting for review their Barangay Ordinance No. 4, series of 2009 together with the proof of public hearing conducted by the barangay in connection with', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the Barangay Resolution No. 20, series of 2008, of MRR Queen of Peace Barangay enacting Ordinance No. 4, series of 2009, entitled ?Barangay ordinance on taxes, fees, clearances and other charges for services rendered all and within Barangay MRR Queen of Peace, Baguio City and for other purposes, which was returned to Punong Barangay Catherine A.  Qui?ones on 24 February 2010, without prejudice to its resubmission together with the proof of a mandatory public hearing conducted for such purposes, as evidence of compliance with Section 186 of the Local Government Code, which mandated that ordinances levying taxes, fees or charges shall not be enacted without any prior public hearing conducted for the purpose, per recommendation of the Committee on Ways and means and Finance, Cluster C, acted upon during the 22 February 2010 Regular Session.)', 'Committee on Ways and Means and Finance (Cluster C: Review of barangay Budgets and Barangay Tax Ordinances; Accreditation of NGOs and other concerns)', '1st', '2010-07-04', '00318-10', 'Considering that the foregoing ordinance showed compliance with Section 186 and 187 of the Local Government Code mandating that ordinances levying taxes, fees, or charges shall be the subject of a public hearing prior to its enactment, as could be evidenced by the hereto attached minutes of the meeting and attendance to the general assembly, the Committee on Ways and Means and Finance, Cluster C, recommends FAVORABLE REVIEW  of the above mentioned barangay ordinance. (CR NR. 00318-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved - FAVORABLE REVIEW (26 Apr 2010, 53)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3136, '2010-05-04', '11:20:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Ms. Mary Padupad', 'Letter dated 30 March 2010 of Ms. Mary Padupad to Hon. Isabelo B. Cosalan Jr., requesting assistance regarding her problem over her titled property at Holy Ghost Extension Barangay, Baguio City.', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '2nd', '2010-07-04', '0601-10', 'Considering that a Notice of Demolition with Non-Compliance Report had been issued relative to the above matter and with the failure of the parties to implement what has been agreed upon during the June 11, 2010 dialogue, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends that the matter be FORWARDED to the City Legal Office, Baguio City for appropriate action and to the BARANGAY COUNCIL, Holy Ghost Extension Barangay, Baguio City for information and guidance. (CR NR. 0601-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-09-08', 'FORWARDED to the Office of the City Legal Officer thru Atty. Melchor Carlos B. Rabanes,OIC, Baguio City, for appropriate action; and\r\nForwarded to the Holy Ghost Extension Barangay, Baguio City, thru Punong Barangay Pio B. Cosape, for information and guidance (09 Aug 2010, 42)', '4th', '2010-11-08', 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
