(3146, '2010-06-04', '04:55:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr.  Johnny N. Chotrani,  President and CEO, ACE Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation', 'Letter dated 29 March 2010 of Mr.  Johnny N. Chotrani,  President and CEO, ACE Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation to then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., requesting indorsement to the City Council the draft Memorandum of Agreement betwe', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is related to the following which were included in the 05 April 2010 Regular Session of the Sangguniang Panlungsod (unfinished business):\r\n[a]   Letter dated 19 March 2010 of Mr. Johnny N. Chotrani,  President and CEO, ACE Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, requesting the following:\r\n                  a.   to present the descriptive details of their technology; and \r\n                  b.  the presence of Mr. Ruben Cervantes, Chair Technical Working Group on Solid Waste Management Technologies and  Ms. Cordelia C. Lacsamana, OIC-Department Head, City Parks Management Office (CPMO).\r\n             (NOTE:  With marginal notation of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as  ?Jun, Please   include  in the next Session Calendar-April, 2010?.\r\n[b] Letter dated 15 March 2010 of  Mr. Johnny N. Chotrani, President and CEO, ACE Technologies, Holdings & Development Corporation to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, regarding the following which was forwarded to the Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology  and  Environmental Protection, Handicapped  and  Differently-Abled Persons on 16 March 2010:\r\n          a.	reiterating their position to pursue their previous proposal and to comply with the criteria embodied in Resolution No. 480, series of 2009; and \r\n          b.        informing that their proposal was not included in the list of proponents evaluated by the Technical Working Group on alternative Solid Waste Management Technologies.', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons', '3rd', '2010-08-04', '00348-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that the above be consolidated with Item 48 of April 12, 2010 Agenda which was not taken up during the last Regular Session dated 26 April 2010. The committee further recommends that the above be NOTED considering that the Technical Working Group of the Solid Waste Management is coming up with the final evaluation of the proposals submitted to them. The committee also suggests that the Technical Working Group shall inform all the proponents including ACE Technologies to avoid repetition of the subject matter. (CR NR. 00348-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (17 May 2010, 50)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3147, '2010-06-04', '04:55:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Romeo D. Concio, City General Services Officer, City General Services Office', 'Letter dated 06 April 2010 of Mr. Romeo D. Concio, City General Services Officer, City General Services Office to then City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista Jr., submitting his report on the use and operation of the Multipurpose Hall, City Hall Annex, Baguio Ci', '-none-', '-none-', 'furnished to the Honorable Members & Research  Div. (attach as supp. doc. of Ord. No. 36, s. 2006)', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', 'Research Division', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3148, '2010-06-04', '04:31:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Santiago M. Bartolome, Secretary to the Sanggunian, Sablan, Benguet', 'Letter dated 29 March 2010 of Mr. Santiago M. Bartolome, Secretary to the Sanggunian, Sablan, Benguet, transmitting the Sangguniang Bayan Resolution No. 10-30 of Sablan, Benguet, entitled ?Resolution disapproving the request of the City of Baguio for a fa', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons', '2nd', '2010-08-04', '00345-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that the above be merely NOTED. (CR NR. 00345-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (17 May 2010, 47)', '4th', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3149, '2010-06-04', '04:31:00', '-none-', 'Faxed letter', 'Ms. Emelita C. Aguinaldo, Officer-In-Charge, National Solid Waste Management Commission (NSWMC)-Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)', 'Faxed letter dated 06 April 2010 of Ms. Emelita C. Aguinaldo, Officer-In-Charge, National Solid Waste Management Commission (NSWMC)-Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) to Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as, clarifying issues on the propo', '-none-', '(NOTE:  The above matter is in reply to the letter dated 25 March 2010 of the City Secretary requesting Hon. Horacio C. Ramos to submit to the City Council a report that would answer the queries as contained in the Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0037-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez.)\r\n\r\n(NOTE: a. The above matter is in reply to the letter dated 25 March 2010 of the City Secretary requesting Hon. Horacio C. Ramos to submit to the City Council a report that would answer the queries as contained in the Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0037-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Calling for an investigation in aid of legislation to determine the legality and social acceptability of the Materials Recovery Facility (MRF) located at Wright Park, Lualhati Barangay, Baguio City, and inviting for this purpose, the Honorable Acting Environment Secretary, Eleazar Quinto, of the Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR) or his designated representative, Ms. Cordelia C. Lacsamana, Officer-In-Charge (OIC) of the City Environment and Parks Management Office (CEPMO), Ms. Norma Bustarde, Punong Barangay, Lualhati Barangay, Baguio City, to determine compliance with the provisions of Republic Act 9003 and for other purposes.?\r\nb.	The Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 0037-10 of Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez was returned to the Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons on 30 March 2010, for further study.)', 'Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons for information', '2nd', '2010-08-04', '00347-10', 'The Committee on Health and Sanitation, Ecology and Environmental Protection, Handicapped and Differently-Abled Persons recommends that letters a and b be consolidated. the committee also recommends that the above be NOTED considering that a faxed letter, attached herewith, from Ms. Emelita C. Aguinaldo, Officer-in-Charge of the NSWMC/S the MRF facility constructed at the Wright Park with funding from the Office of the President is intended to be utilized as a transfer station, storage facility, drop off center, composting and recycling facility, drop off center, composting and recycling facility. The constructed MRF located within Wright Park is suitable for its purpose. (CR NR. 00347-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (17 May 2010, 49b)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3150, '2010-07-04', '09:50:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. James  J. Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Operators Drivers Association (LATJODA)', 'Letter dated 05 April 2010 of Mr. James  J. Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Operators Drivers Association (LATJODA), soliciting consideration of the City Council to issue a written approval to operate ?Off Street Parking? at Shell Abanao and Shell Camp All', '-none-', '(NOTE:  a] With marginal notation of Hon. Vice Mayor Daniel T. Fari?as dated 07 April   2010    ?Jun, Please include in the SP Agenda due to the urgency of the subject matter?.\r\n              b]  The above matter is related to the 1st Indorsement dated 05 March 2010 of the Committee on Employment, Livelihood and Cooperatives forwarding for inclusion in the agenda and for proper committee referral the letter dated 03 March 2010 of Mr. James J. Pay-an, President, La Trinidad Jeepney Operators Drivers Association (LATJODA) to Hon. Nicasio S. Palaganas,  which was included during the Regular Session of the Sangguniang Panlungsod on  08 March 2010, and said letter was approved to be included as part of the City Council records for information purposes only.)', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '6th', '2010-08-07', '0620-10', 'The Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation encourages ?off street parking? because it is one of the solution to traffic problem within the Central Business District. Likewise, the Traffic Management Branch (TMB) of the Baguio Central Police Office (BCPO) offers no objection to the said request as it will not affect traffic along Abanao Street considering that limited units will only be allowed at the Abanao Shell station as the loading and unloading area and Naguillian shell Station (fronting Camp Allen) as staging area.\r\n         In view of this consideration, the committee recommends to approve the request of the LATJODA to use Abanao Shell station as its loading and unloading area and Naguillian Shell station as staging area subject to the following conditions:\r\n1. That only two (2) units will be allowed to use the said loading area at Abanao Shell station;\r\n2. That three (3) units will be allowed to use Naguillian Shell station (fronting Camp Allen) as staging area;\r\n3. That the LATJODA must maintain order and cleanliness at all times and comply with the provisions of the Memorandum of agreement (MOA);\r\n4. That the use of the said area will only be good for one month renewable on monthly basis. Provided however that in the event that the use will aggravate traffic along Abanao Street, the city, thru Traffic Management Branch (TMB) will advise LATJODA to look for another ?off street parking? with one week from notice. (CR NR. 0620-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Deferred - returned to the Committee for further study; with Related Motion of Hon. BLFT - Res-196s2010 (23 Aug 2010, 22a)', '4th', NULL, 'Pending; [Formerly indorsed and referred to the same committee, 1st Ind, 08 Jul 2010]', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3151, '2010-07-04', '08:50:00', '-none-', 'Resolution', 'Philippine National Red Cross, Baguio City Chapter', 'Resolution No. 03-2010, of the Philippine National Red Cross, Baguio City Chapter, entitled ?Resolution requesting the City Government of Baguio through the Honorable City Councilors to designate the space fronting the Red Cross office along Harrison Road', '-none-', '-none-', 'Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation', '2nd', '2010-08-04', '0593-10', 'The Philippine National Red Cross plays a vital role in emergency cases that happen in and around the city. Just like other emergency response teams that attend to crises like disaster and accident cases with promptness and immediacy, the PNRC must be provided with the most convenient access in order that it can deliver and discharge the needed services with expediency.\r\n          Thus, one important access facility that the PNRC must have is a reserved ?parking? or holding area for its ambulance units and clients during the availment of blood needs.\r\n           Cognizant of PNRCs? vital role as an emergency response unit, the Committee on Public Utilities, Transportation and Traffic Legislation recommends that the request, designating that space fronting the Philippine National Red Cross-Baguio City Chapter Office along Harrison Road as a reserved ?parking? area for its ambulance units and clients (during availment of blood needs) be APPROVED. \r\n(CR NR. 0593-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved - Res 189s2010 (23 Aug 2010, 12)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon; Forwareded to the Committee on Public Utilities, Transporation and Traffic Legislation for study and recommendation, 4th Ind. 07 Jul 2010;', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3152, '2010-07-04', '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PO', 'Hon. Antonio R. Tabora Jr.', 'Proposed Ordinance Nr. PO 0034-10 of then City Councilor Antonio R. Tabora Jr. ?Re-aligning the amount of P175,000.00 from the 2007 Annual Investment Plan programs/projects/activities listing under Item No. 106 originally intended for ?concrete fence of T', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, '2010-12-04', 'APPROVED on THIRD Reading dispensing with the 1st and 2nd Readings (12 Apr 2010, 57)', '-none-', NULL, 'Acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
