(3863, NULL, '11:40:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. Ilalo Cardinal, Arrorney-in-fact of Ms. Shirley Aquino', 'Letter dated 07 December 2006 of Mr. Ilalo Cardinal, Attorney-in-fact of Ms. Shirley Aquino, reiterating the application of Ms. Shirley Aquino for a space located at the Carinderia Building, either to treat it as a new application or to reopen the matter ', 'Carinderia Building', '(NOTE:  The letter dated 17 February 206 of Ms. Shirley Aquino, requesting then City Mayor Braulio D. Yaranon to endorse favorably the vetoed Resolution Nr. 261, series of 2005 was not favorably acted upon during the 07 August 2006 Regular Session of the Sangguniang Panlungsod for lack of the required number of affirmative votes to override the veto.)', 'Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce', '2nd', NULL, '0546-10', 'The Committee on Market, Trade and Commerce recommends that the above letters be NOTED for the following reasons:\r\n1. Resolution Nr. 261-2005, which earlier approved the space applied for by Ms. Shirley Aquino, was VETOED by then Hon. City Mayor Braulio D. Yaranon.  The Sangguniang Panlungsod failed to muster enough affirmative votes to override the veto;\r\n2. As previously stated, the space being applied for is an unloading area for bulk fish deliveries (?bagsakan?) and a passageway of vendors and buyers.  To award the area will result to pedestrian congestion, reduction or eradication of the ?bagsakan? area and may endanger the market goers in case of an emergency;\r\n3. There are available stalls at the interior section of the Fish Market which can be applied for;\r\n4. There exists an opposition from the legitimate stall holders and members of the Fish Section Association, which supports the maintenance of the area free from any obstructions to fully serve its intended purposes as passageway and ?bagsakan? area.\r\n\r\n(NOTE:  In the 2nd Indorsement dated 23 March 2009 of then Hon. City Mayor Reinaldo A. Bautista, Jr., His Honor returned City Council Resolution Numbered 058, series of 2009  [Forwarding to the Office of the City Mayor the Appeal for Reconsideration of Mr. Ilalo Cardinal on the Denial by the Baguio City Market Authority (BCMA) of his application for the use of the ?Bagsakan Area? at the Baguio City Public Market?], Denying with Finality, the appeal of Mr. Ilalo Cardinal and other applications for the use of the bagsakan area at the Baguio City Public Market, pursuant to Resolution Numbered 010-08 and item no. 4 of the main agenda of the minutes of the meeting on 06 March 2009 of the Baguio City Market Authority.) (CR NR. 0546-10)', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'NOTED (26 Jul 2010, 31b)', '3rd', NULL, 'Acted upon', 'Market, Trade and Commerce 2008', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
(3864, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'PR', 'Hon. Daniel T. Farinas', 'Proposed Resolution Nr. PR 237-06 of Hon. Daniel T. Fari?as and Hon. Perlita L. Chan-Rondez ?Defining the implementing rules and regulations of Ordinance Numbered 05, series of 1995.?', '237-06', '-none-', '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, '-none-', '-none-', NULL, '-none-', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
