(3981, NULL, '00:00:00', '-none-', 'Letter', 'Mr. James Resultay', 'Letter dated  15 January 2007 of Mr. James Resultay, submitting his application over a parcel of land located along Alley 65M, Bugallon Street, Aurora Hill, West Modernsite Barangay with an area of 317 sq. meters which was subject of the application of hi', 'Lot Application', '-none-', 'Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing', '2nd', NULL, 'UPLH-2018-007', 'On February 9, 2018, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing received a letter from Ms. Narcisa R. Rosario in behalf of her brother, Ferdinand G. Resultay requesting for assistance from the Committee Chairman, Councilor Edgar M. Avila for titling of an unregistered parcel of land located at Res. Section \"H\", Aurora Hill, Baguio City, containing an area  of three hundred  seventeen (317) square meters, more or less, and covered by Tax Declaration ARP No. 01-02016-012747 issued by the Assessor\'s Office of the City of Baguio which is related to the same subject matter stated above.  A copy of the SPA is hereto attached.\r\n\r\nThe matter was endorsed by our committee to the Office of the City Planning and Development Office  for inspection and appropriate action or recommendation on February 26, 2018.  The following were stated in the inspection report submitted by Mr. Elias S. Aoanan, Statistician of the CPDO:\r\n\r\n1. The subject lot application of Mr. Ferdinand Resultay is located along West Modernsite, Aurora Hill Barangay, Baguio City;\r\n2. The lot is accessible thru an existing 4.00 meter wide alley from Torres Bugallon St.;\r\n3. Lot No. 11, Block 31 was previously awarded to Asterio Resultay by virtue of City Council Resolution No. 88 dated May 16, 1957, copy of the City Resolution hereto attached;\r\n4. Sps. Asterio Resultay and Isidra Resultay executed a Deed of Donation in favor of their youngest son, Ferdinand Resultay on 14 July 1997 that certain parcel of land particularly described as Lot 11, Block 31 with an area of three hundred seventeen (317) square meters, more or less including a residential structure built thereon, copy of the Deed of Donation is hereto attached;\r\n5. The same lot was applied for by Mr. James Resultay through the City Council dated January 15, 2007;\r\n6. Mr. James Resultay executed a Quitclaim and Waiver of Rights of the same lot in favor of the applicant, copy of Quitclaim and Waiver of Rights is hereto attached;\r\n7. Payment of real property tax of lot and its improvement is up to date per certification of tax non-delinquency issued by the Office of the City Treasurer.\r\n\r\nIn her letter endorsed to the Chairman of the Committee dated March 6, 2017, Engr. Evelyn B. Cayat, City Planning & Development Coordinator recommends favorable approval of the application.\r\n\r\nIn view of the foregoing, the Committee on Urban Planning, Lands and Housing recommends APPROVAL of the request of Mr. Ferdinand G. Resultay for the transfer of rights over  parcel of land located at Res. Sec. \"H\" Lot 11, Block 31, Baguio Workingmen\'s Village, Modernsite Aurora Hill, Baguio City from his late father, Mr. Asterio P. Resultay with an area of three hundred seventeen (317) square meters, more or less. (UPLH-2018-007).', '0000-00-00', NULL, NULL, 'Approved, Res. No. 084, s. 2018 (19 March 2018, 11b).', '-none-', NULL, 'acted upon', '-none-', '2026-06-03 06:33:43'),
